/* combos-love.js — classic script; assigns to window.TD. No ES modules, so file:// works.
   What two cards say together in a reading about love and relationships. For now it covers the pairs of two
   Major Arcana cards (231) and of a Major Arcana card with a Cups card (308), keyed "idA|idB" in
   deck order like combos.js (see TD.pairKey in js/spreads.js); any other pair shows the general
   reading from combos.js, labelled "General reading".
   Written fresh for this demo; a live site edits or replaces them. Loaded only when a reading needs it. */
window.TD = window.TD || {};
window.TD.COMBOS_LOVE = {"major-00|major-01":"Fresh romantic energy and real social skill have arrived together. If you are single, start a conversation with someone you would normally only notice from across the room, and let your ease do the work. If you are partnered, surprise them with a plan you made yourself, not one you ordered.",
"major-00|major-02":"Your gut has been quietly answering a question your head keeps reopening. If you are single, notice who you feel calm around rather than who looks best on paper. If you are together, say the thing you have sensed but never spoken, gently and without accusation, and see how it lands.",
"major-00|major-03":"A new attachment grows best when both people feel looked after. If you are single, choose dates that feel nourishing, like a shared meal or a long walk, over ones designed to impress. If you are together, do one small tender thing for their comfort and yours, and skip the grand gesture.",
"major-00|major-04":"Openness wants a few ground rules. If you are single, know your non-negotiables before the first date so excitement cannot talk you out of them. If you are together, agree on how you will handle one practical thing you keep drifting on, such as time, chores or plans, and write the answer down.",
"major-00|major-05":"A brand-new connection may be moving toward a traditional shape, such as meeting families, marking milestones or sharing customs. If you are single, ask whether you truly want the familiar script or just assumed you should. If you are partnered, choose which rituals to keep and which to invent.",
"major-00|major-06":"You are being asked what you actually value, and honest answers matter more than chemistry alone. If you are single, decide two or three things you will not compromise on, then date with those in mind. If you are together, tell your partner one hope you have held back, and invite theirs.",
"major-00|major-07":"Excitement has found a direction, so the question is where you are heading, together or alone. If you are single, say what kind of relationship you want instead of drifting into whatever appears. If you are partnered, choose one shared goal for the next few months and check in on it monthly.",
"major-00|major-08":"New love, or a new phase of an old one, rewards gentleness over gusto. If you are single, let attraction grow at its own pace and be kind to your nerves on the first few dates. If you are together, meet a shaky moment with warmth rather than trying to win it, and watch how quickly tension eases.",
"major-00|major-09":"Before jumping into something new, a stretch of solitude may show you what you truly want from a partner. If you are single, treat time alone as useful rather than a waiting room, and finish one honest list of needs. If you are together, ask for a quiet evening and offer the same in return.",
"major-00|major-10":"Timing is doing part of the work here, and no amount of effort can hurry another person's readiness. If you are single, keep living your life so that chance can find you. If you are together, notice that a season is shifting and meet it with curiosity instead of resistance.",
"major-00|major-11":"Honest accounting is called for. If you are single, look fairly at your patterns: what you choose, what you overlook and what keeps repeating. If you are together, talk about whether the give and take feels even, using specific examples instead of scorekeeping. Fairness is a good foundation for anything new.",
"major-00|major-12":"A new stretch of love may ask you to slow down and see it from the other person's side. If you are single, resist pushing for a label this week and stay curious about who they really are. If you are together, describe their view of a recurring argument before you defend yours.",
"major-00|major-13":"An old pattern or relationship chapter is ending so something new can begin. If you are single, drop the story that you are behind or that the same disappointing type will keep turning up. If you are together, name one habit you are both ready to retire, and celebrate its going.",
"major-00|major-14":"New love does better at a steady simmer than a rolling boil. If you are single, let a connection unfold over several meetings without deciding too soon what it means. If you are together, mix novelty into your familiar routines one small change at a time, and see what blend suits you both.",
"major-00|major-15":"A new attraction may be tangled up with an old hook, such as a familiar type, a taste for intensity or a fear of being alone. If you are single, notice whether what pulls you feels warm or merely urgent. If you are together, name one stuck habit without blame.",
"major-00|major-16":"A sudden shake-up may clear away an assumption in your love life and leave room for something more honest. If you are single, let go of a hope built on wishes rather than facts, and stay open to a different kind of connection. If you are together, meet the rough patch with candor.",
"major-00|major-17":"Gentle hope returns after a sore patch. If you are single, trust again in small steps without demanding certainty from someone new. If you are together, do something quietly restorative as a pair, like a long walk or an evening without screens, and let closeness come back at its own speed.",
"major-00|major-18":"A hopeful new connection may be wrapped in half-facts and projected feelings. If you are single, enjoy the mystery without treating your imagination as evidence, and ask direct questions early. If you are together, say a worry aloud instead of letting it grow in private, and compare it with what your partner actually says.",
"major-00|major-19":"Warm, open, uncomplicated affection is on offer. If you are single, say yes to easy, cheerful invitations and let someone meet the sunny version of you. If you are together, plan something playful out in the open, like a day trip or a game night, and enjoy it without analyzing it.",
"major-00|major-20":"A call is asking you to review your romantic history honestly and then begin again as a wiser person. If you are single, forgive yourself and past partners for old mistakes, and date from what you learned. If you are together, revisit an old hurt, apologize where it is due and open a new chapter.",
"major-00|major-21":"One stage of your love story has finished properly, and you are free to begin another. If you are single, count what you learned from past relationships and carry it forward lightly. If you are together, celebrate what you have completed as a pair, then choose a new shared adventure to look forward to.",
"major-00|cups-01":"An open heart is the theme, and something tender is being offered. If you are single, say yes to warmth without demanding a guarantee, and be honest about what you feel. If you are together, share a feeling you have kept to yourself and welcome theirs. Affection given freely is the best possible start.",
"major-00|cups-02":"Two people stepping toward each other at the same speed is the picture here. If you are single, look for reciprocity and notice whether interest is returned as well as offered. If you are together, meet a small disagreement halfway and enjoy how easy it feels. Mutual effort is the sign of a good start.",
"major-00|cups-03":"Friends may be the way in. If you are single, accept invitations to group events, since someone you meet through people you trust is a good start. If you are together, spend time with the friends who are glad for both of you, and let that gladness remind you what you enjoy about each other.",
"major-00|cups-04":"Boredom with your current situation may keep you from noticing a gentle invitation. If you are single, look up from your phone and your routine, since someone kind may already be nearby. If you are together, ask what would make the relationship feel fresh, and try one small change this week.",
"major-00|cups-05":"A past disappointment is still taking up space, and you are allowed to grieve it. If you are single, mourn the person or the plan that did not work out, then turn to the possibilities that remain. If you are together, name a hurt you both carry, and choose one small kindness that moves you forward.",
"major-00|cups-06":"Nostalgia may be pointing toward what feels safe and sweet in love. If you are single, notice which old joys and kindnesses you would like to bring into a new relationship, and look for someone who shares them. If you are together, revisit a favorite early memory and recreate a small piece of it.",
"major-00|cups-07":"Many romantic possibilities are floating around, and few are concrete. If you are single, choose one person or one kind of connection to get to know properly, since daydreams cannot show up for dinner. If you are together, turn a vague wish, such as a trip or a talk, into a specific plan.",
"major-00|cups-08":"Leaving something that no longer feeds you can be an act of self-respect. If you are single, let go of a hope or a habit that has been quietly draining you, and walk toward what you truly want. If you are together, ask honestly whether you both still get what you need, and say it kindly.",
"major-00|cups-09":"A comfortable, happy season is a fine place to begin something. If you are single, enjoy your own company first, and let your wish for love come from fullness rather than loneliness. If you are together, name one thing you wish for the two of you and say it in a light, hopeful way.",
"major-00|cups-10":"A new beginning in love does not have to mean leaving your people behind. If you are single, look for someone who fits into your life instead of someone you would need to hide it from. If you are together, picture the home and rituals you would like, and take one step toward them this week.",
"major-00|cups-11":"A soft, surprising message may arrive, or you may be the one to send it. If you are single, follow a small romantic impulse, like a note or a shared song, and keep it light. If you are together, offer something sweet and a little silly. This can also describe a gentle, sensitive person in your life.",
"major-00|cups-12":"A charming invitation is on the table, and it can be lovely if you ask one practical question too. If you are single, enjoy the attention and notice whether their words and actions match. If you are together, invite your partner to something romantic and specific. This may also describe a dreamy, courteous person, or your own romantic side.",
"major-00|cups-13":"Your emotions are deep, and you can hold them steadily while beginning something new. If you are single, say what you feel honestly and listen closely to what a new person feels. If you are together, offer an evening of calm, attentive listening with no fixing. This may describe an empathic person in your life, or that side of you.",
"major-00|cups-14":"Warmth and good judgment work well together at the start of a relationship. If you are single, be generous and kind while keeping your standards, and notice whether the other person does the same. If you are together, handle a tense topic in a calm, caring tone. This may describe a steady, wise person, or your own settled side.",
"major-01|major-02":"Action and intuition together point to a relationship where you say what you feel and back it with what you do. If you are single, trust your gut about who deserves your time and make a move on it. If you are together, follow a quiet hunch with a direct, kind question.",
"major-01|major-03":"Attention and warmth grow a bond. If you are single, put your effort into dates that let you relax and enjoy the company, like a meal you cook together or a garden walk. If you are together, make something as a pair, such as a dinner or a home project, and look after each other's comfort as you do.",
"major-01|major-04":"Ideas and boundaries go hand in hand. If you are single, clarify what you want and where your limits are, then present yourself with confidence. If you are together, use your creativity to design a routine that works, such as a weekly plan for time together, and stick to it. Structure can make room for spontaneity.",
"major-01|major-05":"Charm works better when it rests on good foundations. If you are single, learn from couples you respect and notice which habits keep their relationships steady. If you are together, honor a tradition or ritual that matters to you both and add a personal twist. Old wisdom and fresh effort make a strong pair.",
"major-01|major-06":"You have real ability to shape your love life, and now comes the question of what you want. If you are single, choose based on values and honest attraction instead of ease. If you are together, make a clear, wholehearted choice to give your partner your attention, and say aloud what you are choosing.",
"major-01|major-07":"Intention and drive make a powerful pair. If you are single, decide what you want in a relationship and take active steps toward it, like joining a group or arranging a date. If you are together, agree on a shared direction and set a goal for the next few months. Steady aim beats scattered effort.",
"major-01|major-08":"Gentle skill outperforms force in relationships. If you are single, let your confidence show in a relaxed way, and let a slow start be fine. If you are together, handle a difficult moment calmly and skillfully, with warmth and no show of power. Steady, kind presence wins trust better than clever lines.",
"major-01|major-09":"Time apart, or quiet within a relationship, can sharpen what you offer. If you are single, spend a few evenings working out what you want, then return to dating with a clear question in hand. If you are together, ask for solitude without making it a statement about your partner, and share what you learned afterward.",
"major-01|major-10":"You can put yourself in the way of luck, and you cannot schedule it. If you are single, be visible and prepared with an open mind, by joining things you enjoy and starting conversations. If you are together, adapt to a change in circumstances as a team, using your best skills. Some timing is not in your hands.",
"major-01|major-11":"Honesty and fairness have consequences, and you have the skill to use them. If you are single, present yourself truthfully, without exaggeration, and expect the same. If you are together, discuss how decisions are shared, and give specific examples of what feels fair. Straightforward dealing is the most reliable way to build trust.",
"major-01|major-12":"A pause may work better than a push. If you are single, stop trying to engineer a meeting or a reply, and look at your dating life from a different angle. If you are together, try to see a recurring issue as your partner sees it, and set your solutions aside until you have listened fully.",
"major-01|major-13":"Ending something old is a creative act. If you are single, clear out habits, messages or expectations left over from a past relationship, and see what space opens. If you are together, agree to retire one pattern that no longer serves you, then decide together what to build in its place.",
"major-01|major-14":"Patience and small adjustments do more than dramatic gestures. If you are single, blend your life with someone else's slowly, and pay attention to how the mix feels. If you are together, test small changes in how you spend time or handle chores, then adjust the proportions until the balance suits you both.",
"major-01|major-15":"Your charm can serve you or trap you. If you are single, notice whether a pattern of flirting, testing or controlling keeps you from real closeness, and try being plain instead. If you are together, ask honestly what habit or need for control you both keep feeding, and loosen it together.",
"major-01|major-16":"A sudden shake-up may reveal that something was built on false footing. If you are single, take a breath and separate what was true about a past connection from what you wished were true. If you are together, meet the disruption with honesty, and rebuild on what was real between you.",
"major-01|major-17":"Hope is quiet and practical. If you are single, act on your trust that things can heal, with small steps like reaching out to a friend or trying a new activity. If you are together, do a modest repair, such as apologizing for something small or resuming a shared habit, and let goodwill return in its own time.",
"major-01|major-18":"Fog makes it easy to build on something imagined. If you are single, ask a new person direct questions about their availability and intentions, and check the answers against their actions. If you are together, confirm a worry with facts before acting on it. What is still murky deserves patience.",
"major-01|major-19":"Affection and honesty are on full display. If you are single, be openly yourself and enjoy meeting people without a script. If you are together, share your joy and your talents with your partner, and celebrate what is going well. There is nothing to hide, and being visible tends to draw good company.",
"major-01|major-20":"A call to use your abilities more fully may extend to your love life. If you are single, review your past relationships honestly, forgive what needs forgiving and date as the person you have become. If you are together, revisit a conversation you have put off, and answer it as your whole self.",
"major-01|major-21":"Something you started has come around to completion. If you are single, mark the end of a long chapter of searching or healing, and enjoy being whole before you begin again. If you are together, celebrate a milestone or shared goal, and write down what you learned about working as a team.",
"major-01|cups-01":"A feeling is offering itself, and you have the skill to give it shape. If you are single, say what you actually want when someone asks. If you are partnered, turn a warm impulse into an action this week: a plan, a note, a small ritual that belongs only to the two of you.",
"major-01|cups-02":"Both of you are bringing something real to the table, and it shows. If you are single, you may meet someone who matches your effort instead of your mystery. Together, stop hoping the other person guesses and say the specific thing you need. Clear asking makes mutual feeling easier to build on.",
"major-01|cups-03":"Your social circle is where the spark may show up, so say yes to the gathering. If you are single, host something yourself and introduce people to each other. In a relationship, plan a night that mixes your two worlds and see how easily it goes.",
"major-01|cups-04":"You have plenty on offer and still feel flat about it. Before you decide the relationship, or the dating pool, has nothing left, try changing what you do together rather than who you do it with. Book something unfamiliar. Boredom sometimes means the routine needs a fresh hand.",
"major-01|cups-05":"Grief over what spilled is real, and you still hold more than you are counting. If a relationship ended or went wrong, let yourself feel it, then look at what remains: your own skills, your friends, your ability to begin again. Single or not, one small act of self-kindness today counts as progress.",
"major-01|cups-06":"An old kindness or a familiar face brings sweetness, and you get to decide what to do with it. If single, notice whether you keep comparing new people to someone from the past. If partnered, recreate a happy early ritual on purpose: the first restaurant, the old playlist. Use memory as material, not a map.",
"major-01|cups-07":"Daydreams about many possible partners, or many versions of your relationship, are crowding out one real conversation. Pick the one thing you truly want and test it in the open. If single, go on the actual date instead of imagining ten. If together, turn a fantasy into a plan you both agree on.",
"major-01|cups-08":"Leaving something behind can be a skilled and deliberate act, not a failure. If a relationship no longer feeds you, you have the clarity to say so plainly and kindly. If you are single, you may be stepping away from a pattern, such as always choosing the unavailable. Decide what you are walking toward as well.",
"major-01|cups-09":"Contentment is available, and you help create it. If you are partnered, notice what you built together and say thank you for it. If you are single, your satisfied energy is attractive on its own, so do not rush toward someone just to fill a gap. Wish clearly, then take one step toward it.",
"major-01|cups-10":"You have the ability to build the shared life you imagine, one action at a time. If single, picture the kind of home and people you want around you, then make choices that fit that picture. If partnered, plan a family gathering, a tradition or a shared goal together. Belonging is made, not only found.",
"major-01|cups-11":"A tender message or first flutter of feeling is here, and your job is to answer it with real words. If single, send the sincere note instead of the clever one. If partnered, write something small and honest that you have been holding back. The Page can be a shy person in your life, or the shy part of you.",
"major-01|cups-12":"An invitation, a romantic gesture or a charming person is in the picture. Enjoy the offer, and watch whether words and actions match over several weeks. The Knight can be someone in your life or the romantic in you. If you are the one offering, follow the flourish with something practical and dependable.",
"major-01|cups-13":"Steady emotional depth meets real skill in how you show up. The Queen may be a caring person in your life or the caring side of you. Use your words and actions to make someone feel safe, and be willing to receive the same. If you are single, gentleness with yourself is a good place to start.",
"major-01|cups-14":"Feelings guided by good sense make for solid footing. The King may be a calm, kind person in your life or the calm, kind side of you. Speak about what hurts without drama, and then act on your words. If single, look for steadiness over intensity. If together, make promises small enough to keep.",
"major-02|major-03":"Your body already knows how you feel about this person, or about this stretch of being alone. Before analyzing, notice what settles you and what tightens you. Then care for that feeling with something small and physical: a shared meal, a slow evening, a walk without your phone.",
"major-02|major-04":"Some feelings are hard to say and some boundaries are hard to hold, and you may be facing both. Name privately what you need, then put one clear limit into words. Private knowing gets sturdier once it has a shape. Single or partnered, a calm sentence beats a long silence.",
"major-02|major-05":"Inner knowing and shared expectations may not agree right now. Maybe family, culture or 'how relationships are supposed to go' pulls one way while your gut pulls another. Listen to both without rushing to pick. Talking with someone you trust about what you actually want can help sort borrowed rules from your own.",
"major-02|major-06":"A choice is forming, and your quietest feeling has the honest answer. Ask what you would choose if nobody were watching or judging. If you are single, that may mean deciding what kind of connection you want. If you are partnered, it may mean saying something you have kept private.",
"major-02|major-07":"Drive and stillness are pulling in different directions. One part of you wants to push things forward, and another says not yet. Slow down long enough to hear the second voice. Moving toward a person or a decision works better when your pace matches what you privately know.",
"major-02|major-08":"Gentle patience is the way in. A tender or guarded feeling, yours or someone else's, will not respond to pressure. Stay calm, stay kind, and let trust be earned slowly. If you are single, this can mean being gentle with your own pace of opening up.",
"major-02|major-09":"Time alone is doing real work right now. You may be sorting out what you want before you let anyone else weigh in. That is not avoidance if you come back with an honest answer. Give yourself a set stretch of solitude, then share what you found with someone safe.",
"major-02|major-10":"Things are shifting in ways you cannot force, and part of you already senses which way. Stop trying to control the timing. Listen for what feels true as circumstances change, and let it guide small choices. Single or attached, you can prepare without grasping.",
"major-02|major-11":"Honesty has to run both ways here, starting with the version you tell yourself. Look at what you have actually done, said and allowed, not just what you felt. Then speak plainly about it. Fairness in a relationship begins with an accurate inner ledger.",
"major-02|major-12":"A pause is not a failure. Something in the connection, or in you, needs to be held still so you can see it from another side. Resist filling the silence with quick answers. Ask yourself what looks different if you drop your usual story about it.",
"major-02|major-13":"Something in your emotional life is ready to end, and you probably felt it before you admitted it. Honor that quiet sense rather than arguing with it. Clearing out an old pattern, hope or habit leaves room. If you are single, that space may be the whole point.",
"major-02|major-14":"Slow, steady blending is what this asks for. Trust develops through small, repeated exchanges, not big declarations. Keep listening to your own feelings while making room for another person's. Go at an even pace, neither rushing nor freezing, and let closeness build.",
"major-02|major-15":"You know more about this pattern than you admit. Something keeps a hold on you, maybe a person, a habit or an old hurt, and part of you has already seen it. Say it aloud to someone safe. Naming the loop is the first step toward loosening it.",
"major-02|major-16":"A sudden jolt may confirm what your gut had been whispering. Something built on a shaky assumption falls, and the shock is real. Give yourself room to feel it. Afterward, notice that you had sensed the crack, and trust that sense earlier next time.",
"major-02|major-17":"Healing here happens quietly, out of sight. You do not have to announce that you are ready to open up again. Rest, be kind to yourself, and let trust return at its own speed. If you are single, hope can be a private and gentle thing.",
"major-02|major-18":"Feelings are muddy right now, and deciding tonight would only add to the fog. Notice what you keep dreaming about, hoping for or fearing, and keep it separate from what has really happened. Ask direct questions and write down the answers you get. Clarity comes with time.",
"major-02|major-19":"What you have felt privately can finally step into daylight. Warmth and honesty go together here: say the true thing cheerfully, without hedging. A relationship benefits from openness, and if you are single, being yourself in plain view is attractive. Enjoy simple time together.",
"major-02|major-20":"An honest review is due, and you already know what it will say. Look back at the whole story of this relationship or your time alone, then answer the call you have been hearing. Forgive what needs forgiving, including yourself, and decide what comes next.",
"major-02|major-21":"A long emotional cycle is nearing its close, and you understand it better than you did. Take time to acknowledge what you have learned about love and about yourself. Whether you are single or partnered, this is a moment for calm gratitude before the next chapter.",
"major-02|cups-01":"Something in your heart is opening quietly, and you may sense it before you can explain it. Give it room without announcing it. If you are single, notice who you feel calm around, not just excited by. In a relationship, sit in comfortable silence together for a while and see what rises.",
"major-02|cups-02":"A connection that feels understood without many words is possible. If partnered, you may both know things the other has not said, so ask gently instead of assuming. If single, trust the person who makes you feel at ease when you are quiet. Mutual feeling does not always announce itself loudly.",
"major-02|cups-03":"Everyone around you seems to be celebrating, and you are watching quietly. That is fine. If single, notice who you are drawn to at the gathering without saying a word, then say one word later. If partnered, you may treasure a private moment more than the party. Your inner life deserves honoring too.",
"major-02|cups-04":"You may feel oddly unmoved by what is offered, and your inner voice is trying to say why. Instead of forcing yourself to feel more, ask what is missing. Alone time helps. Single or partnered, a few quiet days of honest reflection can tell you whether this is boredom, tiredness or a real signal.",
"major-02|cups-05":"Sadness about a loss has a quiet lesson underneath it. Give yourself private time to grieve without explaining it to everyone. In time you may notice what the ending taught you about your needs. Single or together, be gentle with yourself and remember that not everything must be understood right away.",
"major-02|cups-06":"An old memory is surfacing, and it carries information about what you long for now. Reflect on what made that time feel safe or tender, then ask how to bring a little of that into today. If single, past kindness shows you your own standards. If partnered, share a memory you have kept private.",
"major-02|cups-07":"Many romantic possibilities swirl, and your intuition is the one voice that can cut through. Quiet the daydreams and ask which option feels calm rather than dramatic. If single, do not chase every thrill. If partnered, treat fantasies as clues about needs, not instructions. What feels true when you are still is usually the better guide.",
"major-02|cups-08":"Something in you already knows it is time to step away from a situation that no longer fits. You may not have words for it yet. Give the feeling a few quiet weeks and see whether it holds. Single or partnered, walking toward what is true is kinder than staying out of habit.",
"major-02|cups-09":"Deep contentment lives in the quiet parts of your love life. You may not need proof or grand gestures. If partnered, enjoy the private understanding you share. If single, appreciate how complete your own company feels and let that be your baseline. What you wish for will be clearer when you are calm rather than needy.",
"major-02|cups-10":"The sense of belonging you long for begins on the inside. If single, get comfortable with your own values and the kind of home life you want. If partnered, spend quiet time together imagining the next few years. A loving circle grows from people who know themselves and are honest about what they need.",
"major-02|cups-11":"A shy, sweet feeling is stirring, and it may be yours or someone else's. Do not push it into words too early. Let it stay small for a while. If single, notice who you think of and smile. If partnered, a short note left where they will find it says more than a speech.",
"major-02|cups-12":"An invitation or a romantic gesture arrives, and your inner sense should get a vote. Charm is pleasant, but notice how you feel afterward: calm, or unsettled. If single, let a person show consistency over time. If partnered, ask for a quiet evening in place of a show. Your gut can tell you what the flowers cannot.",
"major-02|cups-13":"Compassion and intuition run deep here. The Queen may be a wise, gentle person in your life or the tender side of you. You may sense what a loved one needs before they say it. Use that gift kindly and check your read by asking. If single, sensitivity is a strength when paired with clear boundaries.",
"major-02|cups-14":"Calm emotional wisdom is available, either from a steady person around you or from the steady part of yourself. Take your time before responding to a hard feeling. Quiet reflection turns strong emotion into something you can speak about clearly. Single or together, choose patience over reaction and see how much better conversations go.",
"major-03|major-04":"Warmth and boundaries can support each other. Affection grows best where both people know what is expected and what is off the table. If you are together, talk about routines and limits kindly. If you are single, look for someone who is both caring and dependable.",
"major-03|major-05":"Old family patterns and traditions shape how you give and receive care. Notice what you inherited: how affection was shown, what was expected of partners. Keep the customs that nourish you and gently rewrite the ones that do not. Shared rituals can be a lovely way to bond.",
"major-03|major-06":"Affection and real choice come together here. You are being asked what you value in love, and your body and heart likely already lean one way. Choose the connection that feeds you, and treat it generously. Single or attached, care for what matters most to you.",
"major-03|major-07":"Care and momentum work together when you keep them in balance. You can move toward what you want while staying tender with yourself and others. Avoid pushing so hard that the relationship becomes another task. Let some plans be enjoyable rather than efficient.",
"major-03|major-08":"Tenderness is your strongest tool. With yourself or a partner, patience and kindness are what change things, not pressure. Let affection be steady and unshowy. If you are single, treat your own needs with the same gentleness you would offer a friend.",
"major-03|major-09":"Rest and solitude may be what nurture you most right now. Taking space is not rejection, it is refilling. Tell the people close to you what you need, and be kind to yourself about it. Sometimes the caring thing is a quiet evening with a lamp and a book.",
"major-03|major-10":"Seasons change in relationships, and this looks like a turn toward more abundance. Let good things come without gripping them. Enjoy what is present, and stay flexible about how it unfolds. If you are single, being open to unplanned meetings and ordinary kindness serves you well.",
"major-03|major-11":"Generosity works best when it is fair. Check whether giving and receiving are balanced between you and the other person. Care that only flows one way tends to sour. Speak honestly about what you need, and listen just as honestly.",
"major-03|major-12":"Slowing down lets affection deepen. You may be asked to hold still and let the relationship, or your feelings, ripen without pushing. See the situation from the other person's side. Sometimes the most loving act is to pause and wonder what they need.",
"major-03|major-13":"An old way of loving is ending so a fuller one can grow. Let go of a habit, role or hurt that has stopped nourishing you. Grieve what needs it, then clear space. If you are single, this can be a fresh start with yourself first.",
"major-03|major-14":"A balanced, nurturing rhythm is what serves you. Mix time together with time apart, talking with silence, giving with receiving. Do not rush the middle stretch. Steady, mild care will do more for a relationship, or for your own heart, than intense gestures.",
"major-03|major-15":"Comfort and craving can be hard to tell apart. Notice if something that feels like care is actually a habit that keeps you stuck, such as overgiving or overindulging. Ask what you need beneath the urge. Real nourishment leaves you freer, not more tied.",
"major-03|major-16":"A sudden shake-up may hit what felt safe and cozy. It is unsettling, and it can also clear away something that was not truly feeding you. Look after your basics: sleep, food, friends. Rebuild slowly with what is real and warm.",
"major-03|major-17":"Gentle recovery is underway. After a hard stretch, kindness toward your own body and heart brings hope back in small pieces. Let people care for you and accept it. If you are single, an open, unhurried heart makes room for good things without forcing them.",
"major-03|major-18":"Emotions are rich and a bit foggy. Fertile feelings can also stir old fears and fantasies. Look after your body with sleep and simple meals, and hold off on big conclusions. Ask for what is actually true instead of filling gaps with imagination.",
"major-03|major-19":"Warmth, fun and plain affection are on offer. Enjoy simple pleasures together or on your own: a good meal, sunshine, laughter. Let yourself be openly happy without waiting for a reason. Joy shared freely tends to invite more of it.",
"major-03|major-20":"A moment of honest review asks you to look at how you have loved, including how you have cared for yourself. Forgive where it is due. Then answer the call to live differently: more openly, more warmly. A renewed sense of worth changes how you show up.",
"major-03|major-21":"A loving chapter is coming to a full, satisfying close, or a relationship feels whole and well grown. Savor it. Give thanks, mark the moment together, and rest before you start anything new. If you are single, feeling complete on your own is real.",
"major-03|cups-01":"Love is offering itself in a nourishing form, and you are ready to receive it. If single, allow yourself to be looked after without rushing to repay it. If partnered, a home-cooked meal, a walk outdoors or a long hug feeds the bond better than a big speech. Let affection be simple and generous.",
"major-03|cups-02":"Warm, mutual affection has room to grow. If partnered, tend the relationship like a garden with regular small attention: a meal shared, a hand held, kind words. If single, you may meet someone who cares for you as much as you care for them. Comfort and physical ease are signs of the real thing.",
"major-03|cups-03":"Abundance shows up as a full table and good company. If single, let friends and family be your matchmakers, or simply enjoy being among people who love you. If partnered, host a meal or a small party and share your happiness with others. Affection multiplies when it is passed around.",
"major-03|cups-04":"You have comfort and care all around you, and still feel restless. Look at your body and your routines first: are you tired, under-fed or overbooked? Sometimes a slow morning solves more than analyzing a relationship. Single or together, tend to yourself, then decide whether you need change or simply more rest.",
"major-03|cups-05":"A loss has left you tender, and the answer is care, not analysis. Rest, eat well, and let friends bring you food. Whether the sorrow is about a past relationship or loneliness now, it eases with warmth. When you are ready, notice what still grows in your life: friendships, family, your own kindness.",
"major-03|cups-06":"Nostalgia has a warm taste here: a childhood recipe, an old kindness, the comfort of being known for years. Bring some of it forward by cooking, gardening or visiting family. If single, ask what tenderness you learned early and look for it again. If partnered, tell an old story together.",
"major-03|cups-07":"Many pleasant options, none quite rooted. Ground yourself in everyday life and ask which person or path feels good on an ordinary Tuesday, not just on a romantic evening. If single, choose the one you would happily cook dinner for. If partnered, plan something practical together instead of dreaming alone.",
"major-03|cups-08":"Leaving can be an act of self-care. If a relationship leaves you hungry, you are allowed to look for one that feeds you. Do it kindly, with support nearby: a friend, a place to stay, a plan for the first week. If single, stepping back from draining dates gives you energy for better ones.",
"major-03|cups-09":"A full heart and a comfortable life sit side by side. If partnered, savor small pleasures together: a shared meal, sun on the porch, easy touch. If single, you may be more nourished than you realize, and the wish for love can wait without hurry. Gratitude opens the door wider than urgency does.",
"major-03|cups-10":"Family life and a warm home are at the center. If partnered, nurture the household rhythm: shared meals, holidays, how you care for each other's relatives. If single, your chosen family counts as much as any other. Build a home that feels welcoming to you, and the right company will feel it too.",
"major-03|cups-11":"Something tender is sprouting, so water it gently. If single, a kind message or a shared meal beats a grand declaration. If partnered, small acts of sweetness renew the early feeling. The Page may be a young or shy person in your life, or your own newly opened heart. Let it grow at its natural pace.",
"major-03|cups-12":"A romantic invitation arrives with a generous, sensual flavor. Enjoy the dinner, the flowers or the weekend away, and stay aware of how it feels in the days after. The Knight can be someone in your life or your own romantic side. Single or partnered, let pleasure be a guide while your judgment keeps watch.",
"major-03|cups-13":"Nurturing warmth is abundant here. The Queen may be a loving mother figure in your life or the caring role you play. Give from a full cup, which means resting and being looked after too. If single, treat yourself with the care you would give a friend. If partnered, show love in daily kindnesses.",
"major-03|cups-14":"Generous, steady love with good judgment is the picture. The King may be a dependable, kind person in your life or the reliable side of you. Offer warmth and stability without controlling anything. If single, look for kindness in action. If partnered, share the load at home and talk about needs before resentment builds.",
"major-04|major-05":"Commitment and convention are in focus. You may be weighing what a serious relationship should look like: rules, roles, milestones. Talk openly about which traditions you both want and which you would rather write yourselves. Structure works when both people helped shape it.",
"major-04|major-06":"Choosing someone, or choosing to stay, takes both heart and firm boundaries. Decide what you value, then act on it consistently. Being clear about limits does not cool love, it steadies it. If you are single, know your standards before you meet anyone.",
"major-04|major-07":"Determination and discipline are strong, but relationships need softness too. Check whether you are steering the connection like a project. Agree on a direction together, and leave room for the other person to hold a rein. If you are single, aim at what you want without bulldozing.",
"major-04|major-08":"Firm and gentle can live in the same person. You can hold a boundary without hostility and stay warm while you do it. Try calm words rather than commands. In a relationship, this shows up as steady reliability that also feels safe.",
"major-04|major-09":"Time apart to think about your boundaries may be wise. Step back and ask what structure you need in love, what you can offer and what you cannot. Come back with a clear, honest statement. If you are single, this is a good season for defining your own standards.",
"major-04|major-10":"Even solid foundations sit inside changing seasons. You may want control, and life offers timing instead. Keep your commitments and boundaries steady while allowing feelings and circumstances to shift. Adaptability, paired with reliability, keeps a relationship strong.",
"major-04|major-11":"Fairness and clear terms matter now. Talk about expectations, responsibilities and boundaries with directness. Being consistent and accountable earns trust. If something is unbalanced, say so calmly and propose a fix. Honest rules make room for ease.",
"major-04|major-12":"Control is loosened by willingly pausing. Letting go of the need to steer can reveal what the other person actually needs. Set aside your plan for a while and listen. If you are single, stepping back from rigid expectations may help you notice something new.",
"major-04|major-13":"An old set of rules in your love life is ending. The roles or expectations you built may no longer fit. Let them go calmly and rebuild on honest ground. Singles can drop old standards that came from fear. Partners can write new agreements.",
"major-04|major-14":"Steady, balanced effort builds lasting love. Rules and routines work best when mixed with flexibility. Find a rhythm that suits both of you, and adjust it as life changes. Neither rigid control nor drifting will help. Moderation does.",
"major-04|major-15":"Control can look like security, and that is worth examining. Check whether rules, jealousy or a need to be in charge are holding the relationship in a tight grip, from either side. Real safety includes freedom. Loosen one demand and see what happens.",
"major-04|major-16":"Rigid arrangements can crack suddenly. If a relationship rested on control or unspoken rules, a jolt may expose it. It hurts, and it is also honest. Sort out what was solid and what was only held in place by pressure. Rebuild from the honest part.",
"major-04|major-17":"Hope needs a little structure to last. After a hard time, set gentle routines that help you heal, and keep honest boundaries with people. Trust can return through steady, reliable actions. Singles can hold an open heart alongside clear standards.",
"major-04|major-18":"Feelings are uncertain, and firm decisions now may rest on fog. Hold your boundaries but avoid ultimatums until things are clearer. Ask plain questions, expect plain answers, and notice when your imagination is filling in blanks. Patience protects you.",
"major-04|major-19":"Stability and joy sit comfortably together. A dependable, honest foundation lets happiness show up freely. Enjoy the ease of knowing where you stand. Singles can feel confident in clear values, and partners can celebrate what is working.",
"major-04|major-20":"It is time to review the terms you have been living by. Look honestly at your rules, roles and boundaries in love. Which have served you, and which were fear? Respond to the call to be more honest, and set one new agreement.",
"major-04|major-21":"Something stable and complete has been built. A long effort to create security in love is bearing fruit, or you have finished defining what you need. Appreciate the whole picture. Mark the accomplishment and enjoy the steadiness before the next chapter.",
"major-04|cups-01":"A new feeling arrives and asks for a container. Boundaries do not shrink love, they give it shape. If single, say on a first date what you are open to and what you are not. If partnered, agree on a small weekly ritual and keep it. Structure gives tenderness room to last.",
"major-04|cups-02":"Mutual love does best when both people know the rules of the road. Talk openly about expectations: time, honesty, how you handle disagreements. If single, look for someone who is consistent, not only exciting. If partnered, renew your agreements as life changes. Being met halfway is easier when the halfway point is named.",
"major-04|cups-03":"Friends and community give your love life structure and support. If single, join a regular group with a set schedule, such as a class or a club, and let connection form there. If partnered, set a standing date with friends. Festivity works better with a plan, and a plan can still be warm.",
"major-04|cups-04":"Discontent with the routine may mean it needs a redesign, not a demolition. Look at the frame: how you spend evenings, who handles what, how often you laugh. If single, restructure your week to include something that pleases you. If partnered, propose one change and try it for a month.",
"major-04|cups-05":"After a loss, structure is a comfort. Keep regular meals, sleep and a simple routine while the grief moves through. Single or partnered, set a boundary around what you discuss about the past, and with whom. You can mourn what spilled and still hold firmly to what remains standing.",
"major-04|cups-06":"An old sweetness is worth honoring, but it should not set the rules. If someone from your past reappears, decide on your own terms how much contact suits your life now. If partnered, borrow a good tradition from earlier days and give it a place on the calendar. Memory is a source, not a master.",
"major-04|cups-07":"Fantasies need a filter. List what you truly require in a partner or a relationship, then compare each daydream to that list. If single, decide your limits before you start dating, such as honesty and reliability. If partnered, replace a vague wish with a specific request. Clear standards make choices easier.",
"major-04|cups-08":"Leaving with a plan is different from fleeing. If you have decided a relationship or pattern is not right, set out the steps: what to say, when, and what support you need. If single, walk away from situations that break your own rules. Act with dignity and follow through on what you decide.",
"major-04|cups-09":"Contentment thrives on stable ground. If partnered, protect what works: your routines, your agreements, time for each other. If single, your well-ordered life is a good foundation for meeting someone. Your wish can be met when your boundaries are healthy, so keep them. Gratitude and consistency together are powerful.",
"major-04|cups-10":"A lasting home needs a framework. If partnered, talk about how you divide responsibilities, celebrate holidays and treat each other's families. If single, know the kind of household you want and look for people who share those values. Belonging is easier when the ground rules are kind, clear and mutual.",
"major-04|cups-11":"A shy, tender feeling needs a safe frame. If single, meet in a simple setting with a clear plan, such as coffee at a set time. If partnered, arrange a regular moment for gentle messages. The Page may be a newcomer in your life or a new feeling in you. Give it structure, not pressure.",
"major-04|cups-12":"Any romantic invitation is best met with clear standards. Enjoy the gesture, then ask about what comes next: intentions, timing, consistency. The Knight may be an appealing person in your life or your own romantic side. If single, accept with an open mind and keep your boundaries. Real interest holds up under simple questions.",
"major-04|cups-13":"Deep feeling with firm boundaries makes love sustainable. The Queen may be a compassionate person in your life or the caring role you take on. Care for others without losing yourself: state what you can and cannot give. If single, sensitivity is safest when paired with clear limits. If partnered, ask for what you need directly.",
"major-04|cups-14":"Emotional maturity and reliability are strong together. The King may be a steady, principled person in your life or your own composed side. Handle disagreements with fairness and follow through on promises. If single, look for someone whose kindness is consistent. If partnered, discuss decisions openly rather than issuing them. Authority softens when it is warm.",
"major-05|major-06":"Shared values and recognized commitment come into view. You may be thinking about what vows, traditions or family expectations mean to you. Choose what you honestly believe in rather than what is expected. Then say it aloud to your partner or to yourself.",
"major-05|major-07":"Following a known path can carry you forward. You may feel drawn to conventional milestones, and that is fine when they truly fit. Make sure you are steering, not just being carried. Agree on the route with your partner, and go together.",
"major-05|major-08":"Inherited beliefs about love can be met gently. If old rules, from family or culture, make you anxious or angry, soften toward them without obeying blindly. Patience with yourself and others opens space for new practices. Kindness is a tradition worth keeping.",
"major-05|major-09":"Stepping back from what everyone expects can clarify what you want. Take time alone to sort borrowed beliefs from your own. Reflect on your own ideas of commitment. Later, share your findings with someone wise, whether a friend, counselor or elder.",
"major-05|major-10":"Customs and timing collide. Perhaps people around you expect a schedule for relationships, but life is turning on its own clock. Keep the rituals that hold meaning and let go of pressure. Trust that steady values will carry you through changing seasons.",
"major-05|major-11":"Fair commitments matter more than fancy ones. Check whether the agreements you have, spoken or assumed, are honest and equal. If you follow rules from family or culture, ask whether they treat you fairly. Make your vows real by keeping them, in small ways.",
"major-05|major-12":"Setting aside the expected script allows a new view. You may be asked to pause the usual milestones and question them. Look at the relationship from a different angle. Sometimes stepping out of line for a while shows what you truly believe.",
"major-05|major-13":"An inherited way of doing love is ending. A belief, a role or a family script no longer fits. Let it go respectfully. You can honor what it gave while choosing something more honest. Singles and partners alike can rewrite the rules.",
"major-05|major-14":"Blend what you were taught with what you have lived. Take the best of the traditions you know and mix them with your own experience and your partner's. Go slowly, adjusting as you learn. Healthy commitment is built from steady compromise.",
"major-05|major-15":"Beliefs about how love must look may have become chains. Notice where expectations, guilt or shame keep you in a role that hurts. Question rules you never chose. Talk with someone outside the pattern, and take one step toward a freer arrangement.",
"major-05|major-16":"A belief you inherited about love or commitment may be cracking. It is shocking when a familiar script fails. Give yourself time to feel it. Later, ask which parts of the tradition were real and which were just habit, and rebuild with your own values.",
"major-05|major-17":"Faith in love can return through simple, trusted practices. A gentle ritual, a good conversation with a wise friend, or a shared tradition can restore hope. Take it slowly. Believing in good things again does not require certainty, just a small willingness.",
"major-05|major-18":"Unclear feelings meet familiar expectations. Do not let convention decide for you while you are unsure. Also do not let anxiety rewrite the story. Talk with someone steady and plain-spoken, and take time to see what is real before committing.",
"major-05|major-19":"Shared traditions bring gladness. Celebrations, family gatherings and easy rituals warm a relationship. Do the things that make you both smile. Singles can feel at home in community. Simple, open joy is a fine foundation.",
"major-05|major-20":"A call to reevaluate what you believe about love is loud now. Consider the lessons you were given, review your past, and decide which beliefs you keep. Forgive where needed. Then step into a commitment, or a solo season, that reflects your real convictions.",
"major-05|major-21":"A shared path reaches a celebrated milestone. A commitment, a tradition honored, or a long learning about love comes full circle. Mark it with people who matter. Feel the sense of belonging, then consider what comes next together or on your own.",
"major-05|cups-01":"A tender feeling may want a traditional shape: meeting family, a formal dinner, a commitment ceremony. If you are single, a matchmaking friend or a community group may bring the introduction. If partnered, honor a custom that matters to both of you. Ask what shared ritual would express this opening heart.",
"major-05|cups-02":"Commitment in a recognized form is possible: an engagement, a meeting of families, a shared tradition. If single, you might meet someone through community, faith or a friend's recommendation. If partnered, talk about what vows or rituals would mean to you both. Mutual respect for each other's background deepens the bond.",
"major-05|cups-03":"Celebrations with cultural or family significance are highlighted, like a wedding, a holiday or a community gathering. If single, such events may introduce you to someone who shares your values. If partnered, join in the shared traditions and enjoy belonging to something bigger than the two of you. Ritual helps people feel connected.",
"major-05|cups-04":"Feeling unmoved by convention is worth listening to. Perhaps you are following the expected script for love and it does not fit. If single, ask what kind of relationship you want instead of what people expect. If partnered, consider which traditions still mean something to you both and which are just habit.",
"major-05|cups-05":"Sorrow after a loss may find comfort in shared rituals, community and wise counsel. Talk to a trusted elder, counselor or faith community if that suits you. Single or partnered, you do not need to grieve alone. Someone who has walked this road can help you see what you still have.",
"major-05|cups-06":"Family customs and childhood values return with tenderness. If partnered, consider which traditions from your upbringing you want to keep, and blend them with your partner's. If single, notice the values you learned early and how they shape what you look for. The teachings of your youth can offer comfort and direction.",
"major-05|cups-07":"With many romantic possibilities, tradition offers a filter. Ask what your family, community or faith values, and whether those values matter to you. If single, wise advice from someone with experience can cut through fantasy. If partnered, look at the shared foundation you already have before daydreaming about other paths.",
"major-05|cups-08":"Stepping away from a conventional expectation is the theme. You may be leaving a relationship that fits everyone's idea of right but not your own. Or you may be setting aside a rule about who you should date. Seek wise counsel, then decide by your own values. Honoring your conscience is a tradition worth keeping.",
"major-05|cups-09":"Contentment in a relationship or a life that follows a shared pattern. If partnered, enjoy the comfort of shared values, rituals and community. If single, you may feel satisfied in a life built on principles you believe in. A wish for love is best pursued in a way that respects those principles.",
"major-05|cups-10":"Family, community and shared values combine into a sense of belonging. If partnered, celebrate rites of passage and family gatherings with sincerity. If single, community groups, faith communities or family friends may be a source of connection. Honor the traditions that make you feel part of something, and gently reshape the ones that no longer fit.",
"major-05|cups-11":"A gentle, sincere feeling shows up in an old-fashioned way: a handwritten note, an introduction through friends. The Page may be a young or shy person in your life, or the new-hearted part of you. Single or partnered, let the courtship take its time and respect the pace at which trust forms.",
"major-05|cups-12":"A romantic invitation with serious intentions may be coming. The Knight may be someone offering a traditional courtship, or your own idealistic side. Ask whether their values match yours, not just their charm. If single, it is fine to want a partner who honors what you honor. If partnered, plan a meaningful gesture.",
"major-05|cups-13":"Compassion rooted in values is the picture. The Queen may be a warm, principled person in your life or the caring role you play. Support those you love in ways that reflect what you believe. If single, look for kindness that matches how a person lives. If partnered, let shared beliefs guide you through hard times.",
"major-05|cups-14":"Wise, kind guidance is available. The King may be a trustworthy, principled person in your life or the wise side of you. Handle emotions with maturity and let shared values steer your choices. If single, look for someone whose kindness and principles are consistent. If partnered, discuss big decisions calmly, drawing on what you both hold dear.",
"major-06|major-07":"Decide, then move. You have weighed the choice long enough, and hesitation is now costing you. Pick what fits your values, and act on it with confidence. Partners can agree on a direction and steer together. Singles can take a real step.",
"major-06|major-08":"Love asks for courage and gentleness at once. Choose what you value, and stay patient with the messy parts of a real relationship. Handle your own fears kindly. Tenderness with a partner, or with yourself, is a quiet form of strength.",
"major-06|major-09":"A big choice about love deserves quiet thought. Step away from other people's advice, and ask yourself one honest question about what you want. Take time alone if you need it. The answer you find will be easier to live with.",
"major-06|major-10":"Choices meet circumstances. A meeting, a turning point or a change in timing may bring a decision to your door. You cannot control everything, but you can choose your response. Stay true to what you value as things shift.",
"major-06|major-11":"An honest, fair decision is needed. Look at the facts of the relationship as well as the feelings. Consider how your choices affect both of you. Take responsibility for your part. Clear, truthful communication builds real trust.",
"major-06|major-12":"A choice is on hold, and that pause may be wise. Resist forcing an answer. Look at the situation from your partner's side, or from the side of your future self. Sometimes the right choice becomes obvious after you stop pushing.",
"major-06|major-13":"A choice involves letting something go. To choose one path in love, you may have to end another: an old attachment, a habit, a fantasy. Grieve it, then commit to what you value. Clean endings allow honest beginnings.",
"major-06|major-14":"Harmony develops from patient, equal exchange. Two people, or two parts of you, learn to blend. Keep a steady pace and adjust as you learn each other. Compromise is not losing, it is how a shared life gets built.",
"major-06|major-15":"Attraction and attachment can look alike. Ask whether this connection reflects your values or is running on habit, craving or fear. Notice where you give up power. A healthy bond leaves you freer. Choose what helps you grow.",
"major-06|major-16":"A sudden event tests a relationship or reveals a mismatch. It can be painful, and it also cuts through pretense. After the shock, ask what you truly value. Rebuild, or begin again, on honest ground.",
"major-06|major-17":"Hope and honest connection go together. After a hard time, you can open up to love with clear values and a gentle heart. Trust returns bit by bit. Singles might feel a spark of quiet optimism. Partners can renew their commitment.",
"major-06|major-18":"Confusion clouds a choice. Feelings, dreams and worries mix, and it is hard to tell what is real. Avoid deciding tonight. Ask direct questions, watch actions over words, and give it time. What is true tends to show itself steadily.",
"major-06|major-19":"Open, joyful love is highlighted. A choice made from honest values brings ease. Enjoy each other's company, laugh, and be visible. Singles can bring genuine warmth to new meetings. Couples can simply celebrate what is good.",
"major-06|major-20":"It is time to answer honestly. Look back at your relationship story and choose accordingly. Forgive what needs forgiving, then commit to what you truly want, whether that means deepening a bond or living independently.",
"major-06|major-21":"A relationship, or a stage of self-discovery, reaches wholeness. Two halves feel integrated, or you feel complete on your own. Celebrate. Take time to enjoy the union and to appreciate the choices that led here.",
"major-06|cups-01":"A new love offers itself at a moment of choice. Ask whether it fits what you value, not only what you feel. If single, say yes to someone whose values match yours, or no to someone whose do not. If partnered, choose again, out loud, to open your heart to your partner.",
"major-06|cups-02":"Two people choose each other, and the choice is renewed every day. Talk about your values and whether you are moving the same way. If single, a real match is possible when values align. If partnered, say plainly what you appreciate and what you want to keep building together.",
"major-06|cups-03":"Choices ripple through your social world. Friends may weigh in, and you decide which voices to trust. If single, pick gatherings that reflect who you are and see who shares it. If partnered, think about how your relationship fits with your friends, and choose to celebrate it openly.",
"major-06|cups-04":"You are dissatisfied, and a choice is waiting behind the feeling. Ask what your values are telling you about your current situation. If single, notice whether you are settling or truly unmoved by what is on offer. If partnered, name the part of the relationship that no longer aligns and talk about it directly.",
"major-06|cups-05":"After a loss, you face a choice about how to move forward. Grieve fully, then ask which values you want guiding your next steps. If single, you can choose to open your heart again in your own time. If partnered, decide together how to rebuild trust and what to keep.",
"major-06|cups-06":"Old affection asks you to choose between past and present. A memory can be lovely without being a plan. If single, notice whether you compare everyone to someone from before. If partnered, choose to build new sweet memories together. Decide consciously what to carry forward and what to release.",
"major-06|cups-07":"Many appealing choices, one real decision. Get honest about which values you cannot compromise, and use that to sort the daydreams from the possible. If single, pick the person or path that fits your character. If partnered, talk about a fantasy openly and decide together what to do with it.",
"major-06|cups-08":"You are choosing to leave something behind because it no longer aligns with what you value. That is a legitimate, mature choice. If single, step away from patterns and people who do not match your standards. If partnered, be honest about what you need in order to stay, and what would send you elsewhere.",
"major-06|cups-09":"Satisfaction comes when your choices match your values. If partnered, notice how far you have come by choosing each other, and say so. If single, a wish fulfilled in love depends on staying true to yourself. Enjoy the ease that comes from living in line with what you believe.",
"major-06|cups-10":"A whole, harmonious life comes from choosing what matters. If partnered, talk about the shared future you want and the values behind it. If single, choose the community and people that reflect you. Belonging is built by picking your people and being picked back. Align your daily choices with the home you hope to create.",
"major-06|cups-11":"First feelings bring a first choice: whether to say something. Honesty is the value at stake. If single, tell the person, kindly, that you like them. If partnered, share a vulnerable feeling you have kept quiet. The Page may be a shy person in your life or the newly open part of you.",
"major-06|cups-12":"A romantic offer puts a choice in your hands. Notice whether the invitation matches your values and your pace, not just how flattering it is. The Knight may be a charming person in your life or your own romantic side. If single, say yes or no clearly. If partnered, choose the gesture that says what you mean.",
"major-06|cups-13":"Loyal, deeply felt love is a choice made again and again. The Queen may be a compassionate person in your life or your own caring nature. Choose partners and friends who respect your feelings. If single, let your heart lead while your values keep watch. If partnered, choose kindness in the small moments.",
"major-06|cups-14":"Emotional maturity shows in how you choose. The King may be a steady, wise person in your life or the calm side of you. Make decisions in love by weighing feeling and reason together. If single, choose someone whose actions reflect their words. If partnered, decide as a team and keep your commitments.",
"major-07|major-08":"Determination softens into patience. Rather than pushing a relationship toward a result, steer with a light hand. Let feelings unfold and respond with calm. Whether single or attached, self-control paired with kindness beats forcing the pace.",
"major-07|major-09":"Slowing down from a rush toward love or an outcome may serve you. Pull over, take some solitude, and ask what you actually want. Then move again with clearer intent. Singles can use this pause to focus on self-knowledge.",
"major-07|major-10":"Momentum meets unpredictability. You are trying to steer, and events keep turning. Set your direction, but stay flexible about the route. Not everything in a relationship, or in finding one, follows your timetable. Adapt and keep going.",
"major-07|major-11":"Move forward honestly. Drive toward what you want, but check that you are treating others fairly along the way. Speak clearly and own the impact of your choices. A relationship gains steadiness when ambition and accountability travel together.",
"major-07|major-12":"Forward motion stops, and it may be for a reason. The urge to push a relationship along runs into a necessary pause. Use it to look at things differently. Willing patience now can prevent a rushed choice.",
"major-07|major-13":"A destination you were rushing toward may need to be let go. Endings redirect the journey. Grieve honestly, then choose a new heading. Singles may drop a chase that no longer fits. Partners can end a habit that slowed them.",
"major-07|major-14":"Steady pace wins. Instead of rushing toward a result, move at a moderate speed and keep blending your needs with another's. Small, consistent gestures beat dramatic bursts. Balance ambition with rest, and love has room to develop.",
"major-07|major-15":"Drive can turn compulsive. Check whether you are chasing someone or something out of habit, pride or fear. Real momentum feels chosen. Loosen the chain, take the reins back, and ask what you actually want.",
"major-07|major-16":"A sudden shock stops your momentum. A plan for a relationship, or your idea of it, is disrupted. It is jarring. Let yourself feel it, then check what you can salvage. New direction comes after the dust settles.",
"major-07|major-17":"Renewed hope gives you direction. After a difficult time, gently move toward what feels healing. Take small, steady steps. Singles can set an intention for the kind of love they hope for. Partners can plan something restorative together.",
"major-07|major-18":"You want to move things forward, but the picture is not clear yet. Slow down before you steer. Ask the plain question you have been avoiding, and notice whether your certainty comes from facts or from a mood. If you are single, do not rush toward someone you barely know.",
"major-07|major-19":"Effort and warmth are pulling the same way, which is rarer than it sounds. If you are partnered, choose one shared goal and go after it together, like a trip or a move. If you are single, showing up openly and with energy will serve you better than playing it cool.",
"major-07|major-20":"A moment of honest review asks where this relationship is heading, or what you truly want from dating. Stop drifting. Answer the call with a real conversation, then act on what you hear, even if that means changing course. Direction only counts once someone says it out loud.",
"major-07|major-21":"A long push is reaching its finish. Maybe you worked through a rough patch together, or you finally feel ready after time on your own. Enjoy arriving instead of hunting for the next challenge. Mark the moment with something small and shared, then ask what comes next.",
"major-07|cups-01":"Feelings open, and you want to move. Channel that into action: ask the person out, plan the trip, say the thing. If single, momentum works in your favor once you put yourself in motion. If partnered, pick a shared destination and go, even a small one. Keep both hands on the reins as you speed up.",
"major-07|cups-02":"Two people pulling in the same direction is the picture. Talk about where you both want to go and set a pace together. If single, look for someone whose plans line up with yours. If partnered, work on a shared goal, like a trip or a move. Mutual effort turns affection into progress.",
"major-07|cups-03":"Your social life picks up speed. Say yes to invitations and get out there. If single, a busy calendar brings chances to meet people. If partnered, plan an outing with friends that you both look forward to. Enjoy the ride, and pace yourself so joy does not turn into exhaustion.",
"major-07|cups-04":"You are moving but not feeling. Pull over for a moment and ask what you actually want from love. If single, do not date just to stay busy. If partnered, slow down and look at what the relationship offers you now. Direction matters more than speed, and a break can reveal it.",
"major-07|cups-05":"You have lost something and feel the pull to keep moving. Give the sadness its space, then get back on the road at a pace you can manage. If single, take gentle steps: a walk, a coffee with a friend. If partnered, steer through the hard moment together. Progress and grief can share the car.",
"major-07|cups-06":"Old feelings sit in the rearview mirror, and they are lovely. Look, appreciate, and keep driving. If single, do not turn the car around because of nostalgia. If partnered, borrow a happy memory as fuel for a new adventure together. Progress is possible without pretending the past did not matter.",
"major-07|cups-07":"Lots of romantic roads, and you have one car. Pick a direction and commit to it for a while. If single, choose one person to get to know rather than sampling ten. If partnered, decide on a shared goal and give it your full attention. Determination turns daydreams into a route.",
"major-07|cups-08":"You are driving away from something on purpose, and it takes courage. If a relationship no longer works, act with resolve and kindness. If single, leave old patterns behind and head toward what you want. Keep the wheel steady, know your destination, and do not look back more than the road requires.",
"major-07|cups-09":"Success and satisfaction ride in the same vehicle. If partnered, celebrate what you have both achieved and built. If single, your confidence and drive are attractive. Enjoy the wish coming closer, and keep moving toward it. Contentment does not mean stopping. It means enjoying the ride.",
"major-07|cups-10":"You are steering toward a shared home and a life among people you love. If partnered, plan the next milestone together and work toward it. If single, know that building a warm circle takes direction and effort. Put your drive into the relationships that matter, and enjoy the belonging that results.",
"major-07|cups-11":"A tender feeling is ready to go somewhere. Take the first small step and send the message. The Page may be a shy person in your life or your own new feeling. If single, momentum begins with one action. If partnered, start a small project together, like a walk each evening.",
"major-07|cups-12":"An invitation full of motion is on the table. Enjoy the ride, and keep track of where you are going. The Knight may be a passionate person in your life or your own adventurous side. If single, accept the invitation and watch whether the effort continues. If partnered, plan something spirited together.",
"major-07|cups-13":"Emotional depth meets strong direction. The Queen may be a caring, determined person in your life or those two qualities in you. Move toward what you love with gentleness and resolve. If single, let your sensitivity guide you toward the right people. If partnered, stay steady and kind when the road gets bumpy.",
"major-07|cups-14":"Emotional control and purposeful motion make a strong pair. The King may be a steady, capable person in your life or your own calm strength. Handle strong feelings without letting them steer. If single, look for consistency. If partnered, stay level in disagreements and keep moving toward your shared goals together.",
"major-08|major-09":"Gentleness needs some quiet to grow. Step back from the noise and ask yourself one honest question about what you need. Then bring the answer to your partner, or to your dating life, calmly. Patient self-knowledge makes you kinder and clearer with other people.",
"major-08|major-10":"Some of this is not yours to control, and gripping tighter will not help. Stay warm and steady while circumstances shift, whether that is distance, timing, or someone else's readiness. Offer patience to yourself as well. Let what is real prove itself over time.",
"major-08|major-11":"Kindness and fairness need to travel together here. Speak plainly about what each of you gives and receives, without scorekeeping or blame. Being gentle does not mean being silent. If you are single, look for someone whose actions match their words over many weeks.",
"major-08|major-12":"Waiting is fine when it is chosen and draining when it is not. Ask which this is. Try seeing the situation from your partner's side for a few days without arguing your case. If you are single, a pause can be a gift, provided you use it kindly.",
"major-08|major-13":"An ending is here, and you can meet it without hardening. Grieve honestly, be gentle with yourself, and do not rush to fill the space. If a chapter with a partner is changing form, courage looks like calm truth. If you are single, clearing old hurt makes room.",
"major-08|major-14":"Good relationships are built in the long middle, and this pair knows it. Small daily kindnesses, moderate reactions, and a steady temper do more than grand gestures. If you are single, notice who is easy to be patient with and who blends well with your ordinary life.",
"major-08|major-15":"A pattern has a grip on you, and force will not break it. Notice what you keep returning to even though it costs you, then face it with compassion instead of shame. Small honest steps beat dramatic vows. Ask a friend you trust to hold you accountable.",
"major-08|major-16":"A sudden shake-up tests how steady you are, so react slowly. Something false is falling, perhaps a story you told yourself or a promise that was never solid. Stay kind, protect your dignity, and let the dust settle before you decide what to rebuild.",
"major-08|major-17":"Healing is under way, and it rewards gentle persistence. Keep offering small kindnesses to yourself and to a partner. If you are single after a hard chapter, trust returns gradually. Hope does not need to be loud to be real, and it grows when you keep tending it.",
"major-08|major-18":"Unclear feelings, yours or theirs, tempt you to force an answer. Do the opposite. Stay calm, let your intuition speak without turning it into a story, and give things time to become visible. Be patient with your fears without letting them make the decisions.",
"major-08|major-19":"Warmth comes easily when you are relaxed with yourself. Enjoy the simple good: laughter, affection, an unforced day together. If you are single, your quiet confidence is attractive, so let yourself be seen. Being open usually costs less than you fear.",
"major-08|major-20":"An honest review is calling. Look at how you have handled your own fears and reactions, and answer with courage rather than defensiveness. Forgive yourself for the rough patches, then have the talk that clears the air. A deeper level of trust becomes possible.",
"major-08|major-21":"Patience has carried you to a place of wholeness. Whether partnered or single, you may feel complete in a way that does not depend on anyone's approval. Celebrate that steadiness, and let it shape what you choose next. Nothing is missing from today.",
"major-08|cups-01":"Someone or something is offering you a fresh feeling, and you have the steadiness to receive it without grabbing. If you are single, let warmth grow at its own pace rather than testing it. If you are partnered, a gentle, unhurried gesture of affection will open more than any big declaration could.",
"major-08|cups-02":"Two people meeting each other halfway, with neither forcing the pace. That is a rare kind of trust. Single, look for the person who is gentle with your rough edges. Partnered, patience with a repeated disagreement will bring you closer than winning it ever would.",
"major-08|cups-03":"Friends can be a quiet strength for your love life right now. Being warm and unguarded in a group shows people who you are. If you are single, a gathering may introduce someone kind. If partnered, share your happiness with others and stay gracious when the room gets loud.",
"major-08|cups-04":"Restlessness with what is in front of you deserves gentle honesty, not a hasty exit. Ask whether the flatness is boredom, tiredness or something unspoken. Partnered, plan one small new experience together. Single, notice whether you are ignoring a kind offer because it feels too calm.",
"major-08|cups-05":"Grief over what went wrong is real, and you do not have to rush past it. Yet something is still standing behind you. Be tender with yourself first. Partnered, forgive slowly and say what hurt. Single, healing makes you more open than pretending you are fine.",
"major-08|cups-06":"Old tenderness resurfaces, and you can meet it without being pulled backward. A familiar kindness may remind you what you truly need now. Partnered, revive a sweet ritual from the early days. Single, let nostalgia teach you what you value, then look forward with a settled heart.",
"major-08|cups-07":"Many romantic fantasies are floating around, and only some are real. Steady self-command helps you tell a person apart from the picture you painted of them. Single, spend time with someone in ordinary light. Partnered, talk about what you actually want rather than dreaming beside each other.",
"major-08|cups-08":"Leaving can be an act of courage, and it can also be gentle. If something has stopped nourishing you, you can step away without cruelty or drama. Single, you may be leaving old patterns. Partnered, name your unmet need clearly before deciding whether the way forward is together.",
"major-08|cups-09":"This is contentment earned through patience. You have learned to be at ease with yourself, and it shows. Single, you are not waiting to be completed. Partnered, enjoy the comfort you have built and thank the person who helped build it. Let simple happiness be enough today.",
"major-08|cups-10":"Belonging grows from gentleness repeated over time. Home, family or a circle of chosen people holds you, and your patience helped make it so. Partnered, protect the quiet routines that keep everyone close. Single, you may already have more love around you than you have counted.",
"major-08|cups-11":"A tender message or first flutter of feeling arrives, and you are ready to handle it softly. Do not smother it with expectations. Single, answer warmly and let it unfold. Partnered, a small, sincere note of affection can soothe old tension better than a long discussion.",
"major-08|cups-12":"A romantic invitation comes, charming and sincere on the surface. You have the steadiness to enjoy it while watching how consistent it proves to be. Single, accept the date but let actions build the picture. Partnered, revive courtship: plan an evening that is thoughtful rather than showy.",
"major-08|cups-13":"Deep feeling, held calmly. You or someone near you carries great compassion without being swept away. Single, your sensitivity is a strength, not a flaw to hide. Partnered, listen fully and respond with quiet reassurance. Emotional safety is what lets the closeness between you deepen.",
"major-08|cups-14":"Kindness with judgement is on offer, from someone else or from you. It means feeling deeply and still choosing wisely. Single, look for calm maturity over intensity. Partnered, stay generous but keep honest limits. Steady love does not need to be dramatic to be real.",
"major-09|major-10":"Time alone is not a detour right now, it is part of the turn. Use the quiet to work out what you truly want, because circumstances are shifting. If you are together, ask your partner for space without leaving. If you are single, do not force the timing.",
"major-09|major-11":"Sit alone with a fair question: what have I contributed to this, and what do I deserve? Answer without excuses. That honesty prepares you for a straight conversation with a partner, or a wiser choice about who to date next.",
"major-09|major-12":"Both figures are withdrawn, so this is a rest, not a rejection. Let a stalled situation stay quiet a little longer. Use the still time to look at your habits from the outside. If you are single, a deliberate pause can be a healthy choice, not a failure.",
"major-09|major-13":"An ending invites a stretch of solitude, and that is fine. Give yourself time to sit with what is over without rushing into the next connection. The lamp you carry will show what you want next. Partners can do this inside a relationship, too.",
"major-09|major-14":"Quiet time and gentle balance work well together. Reflect alone, then blend what you learn slowly into your relationship or your dating life. No dramatic announcements are needed. Small adjustments in how you listen and share space will show your growth.",
"major-09|major-15":"Turn the lamp on a habit that holds you. Perhaps it is a pattern with a certain type of person, or a dependence you have excused. Look at it alone and honestly. Seeing it clearly is not punishment, it is how the chain begins to loosen.",
"major-09|major-16":"After a sudden jolt, retreat for a while. You do not owe anyone an instant explanation or a new plan. Sit quietly with what fell, and notice what was never solid. Your lamp will show what is still worth building on.",
"major-09|major-17":"A quiet period is turning toward hope. Time alone has helped you heal, and a gentle openness is returning. You do not need to rush toward anyone. Let your own light steady you, and it will draw the kind of company that suits it.",
"major-09|major-18":"You are searching in dim light, and it is easy to mistake shadows for facts. Go quiet, write down what you actually know versus what you fear, and hold off on big conclusions. Clarity with a partner comes from steady questions, not guesses.",
"major-09|major-19":"Solitude has turned into contentment. Whether you are single or partnered, you feel at ease with yourself, and that shows. Share your happiness simply. A relationship gains a lot from someone who knows their own mind and enjoys their own company.",
"major-09|major-20":"The lamp reveals a truth you have half known. Hear it, and respond. It might be that you are ready to commit, to leave a pattern behind, or to be honest about what you want. Calmly answering this call is worth more than another year of wondering.",
"major-09|major-21":"A period of self-discovery reaches a natural finish. You know yourself better, and that shows in how you relate. If you are single, you can meet others from wholeness, not need. If you are partnered, share what you have learned.",
"major-09|cups-01":"Quiet time has cleared space, and now a new feeling can enter. Do not rush to share it with everyone. Let it be yours for a little while. Single, welcome the gentle stirring. Partnered, one honest question asked softly can open a more tender conversation than months of silence.",
"major-09|cups-02":"Solitude has taught you what you need, which makes real partnership possible. Share what you found rather than keeping it to yourself. Single, meet someone slowly and speak plainly. Partnered, take turns being open about your inner life so closeness does not require constant company.",
"major-09|cups-03":"The pull between retreat and celebration is the story. You want a quiet evening and your friends want you at the party. Go for an hour, leave when you have had enough. Single or partnered, community is warmer when you attend on your own terms.",
"major-09|cups-04":"Withdrawing and feeling indifferent can look alike, so ask yourself which one it is. If you need solitude, say so kindly to the person near you. Single, do not dismiss a gentle invitation out of habit. Partnered, name the flatness aloud, and let one honest question guide you both.",
"major-09|cups-05":"Grieving is often private, and that is allowed. Step back and let the sadness be honest rather than performed. Then let one trusted person in. Single, healing is the work now. Partnered, tell your partner you are hurting even if you cannot yet explain why.",
"major-09|cups-06":"Memory carries a lamp into the past. Old affection or a familiar face can teach you what you always wanted from love. Single, consider what that kindness looked like, then look for it in the present. Partnered, tell the story of your early days and ask for theirs.",
"major-09|cups-07":"Alone time can clear fantasies or feed them, and only honesty tells the difference. Ask which longings are real and which are decorations. Single, write down what you truly want in a partner, in plain words. Partnered, share one wish with your person that you have never said aloud.",
"major-09|cups-08":"Leaving something behind to search inwardly for meaning is the heart of this pair. You are walking away from what no longer feeds you, and solitude is not a punishment. Single, that path is valid. Partnered, tell the truth about why you need space, and for how long.",
"major-09|cups-09":"Contentment that needs no audience. You have learned to enjoy your own company, which makes love a choice rather than a need. Single, savor this stage fully. Partnered, protect time to be alone together in the same room, each at ease and glad of the other.",
"major-09|cups-10":"Belonging and solitude are both needed, and a healthy home honors each. Give yourself and others permission to retreat without it meaning distance. Single, community and family may be your steady love. Partnered, agree on rhythms of time apart and time together so warmth stays easy.",
"major-09|cups-11":"A tender feeling appears, and you want to examine it privately before answering. That is fine. Keep the reply honest and small. Single, notice how you feel about a message, not merely what it says. Partnered, gentle curiosity about your partner's inner world is a lovely gift.",
"major-09|cups-12":"An invitation arrives while you are in a reflective mood. Take a night before answering, and ask yourself one honest question: do I want this, or do I want to be wanted? Single, romance is welcome but not compulsory. Partnered, plan a low-key, thoughtful date.",
"major-09|cups-13":"This is a deeply intuitive, private heart. You or someone close feels more than they say, and the wise response is patience. Single, let trust form quietly. Partnered, give your person time to speak from the depths, and share your own inner life in return.",
"major-09|cups-14":"Emotional maturity often grows in solitude. Someone, perhaps you, has thought carefully about what love requires and can offer it calmly. Single, look for wisdom over fireworks. Partnered, be the one who listens first, and ask a question that helps both of you understand what you need.",
"major-10|major-11":"Fate and fairness meet. Things are turning, and what you have put into a relationship is coming back in kind. Be honest and act decently while the wheel moves. If you are single, how you treat people now shapes who is around you later.",
"major-10|major-12":"Things are turning, yet you feel stuck. Accept that some timing is not yours to hurry. Use the wait to see your situation from another side, perhaps your partner's. If you are single, let the pause teach you what you want, instead of what you think you should want.",
"major-10|major-13":"A cycle is closing and another is beginning. It may feel like loss, but it is also movement. Let an old pattern or connection finish. Endings in love create room for something truer. Take care of yourself while things turn, and stay open to what arrives.",
"major-10|major-14":"Slow blending beats sudden fireworks while circumstances shift. Adjust your pace to the season you are in, and mix openness with patience. Small, steady adaptations with a partner keep things balanced. If you are single, let connections grow at a moderate temperature instead of forcing heat.",
"major-10|major-15":"The wheel keeps turning through the same pattern. Ask why the same kind of situation keeps returning, and what in it holds you. The cycle is not fate, it is a habit dressed as fate. Change one choice and the rotation changes.",
"major-10|major-16":"A sharp turn arrives and old arrangements do not survive it. It may feel unfair, and part of it is simply timing. Look at what was already shaky. You are not powerless: choose how you respond, and rebuild with more honesty than before.",
"major-10|major-17":"After a hard turn, hope returns. Luck seems to be shifting, and you may feel gently optimistic again. Nurture that feeling with honesty and small steps. If you are single, let yourself meet people through ordinary life. If you are partnered, share your renewed trust.",
"major-10|major-18":"Changes are underway, but you cannot see them clearly yet. Avoid acting on moods or midnight worries. Give things time to show their shape, and ask for honest words instead of guessing. Your intuition is useful, but check it against what is actually said and done.",
"major-10|major-19":"Good timing and plain happiness line up. Things feel lucky and easy, so enjoy them with gratitude. If you are single, say yes to invitations and let joy lead. If you are partnered, celebrate together, and remember to appreciate the ordinary good days too.",
"major-10|major-20":"A turning point calls for an honest answer. The situation is moving, and you feel a summons to decide who you want to be within it. Speak the truth you have been holding. Whatever the reply, you will know where you stand.",
"major-10|major-21":"A full cycle closes gracefully. What began some time ago has run its course and reached a satisfying place. Look back with gratitude. If you are single, you feel whole and ready for a new turn. If you are partnered, celebrate how far you have come.",
"major-10|cups-01":"A turn of fortune brings a new feeling into view. You did not plan its timing, and you do not need to. Single, stay open to unexpected introductions. Partnered, welcome a fresh wave of tenderness. Receive it gratefully rather than trying to hold it in place or predict where it goes.",
"major-10|cups-02":"Two people meeting at just the right moment. Whether it is the start of something or a renewed connection, timing helped, but mutual effort will carry it. Single, say yes to a fair invitation. Partnered, greet the changes ahead as a team and keep facing the same direction.",
"major-10|cups-03":"Luck gathers you among friends, and someone in that circle may matter more than you expected. Single, go to the gathering without an agenda. Partnered, share good news and let your circle celebrate you both. Seasons change, so enjoy the warmth of this one openly and gratefully.",
"major-10|cups-04":"Life keeps turning while you sit with your arms folded, and an offer may go unnoticed. Ask yourself if boredom is hiding a real need or if you are turning away from something good. Single, look up. Partnered, do one thing that breaks the pattern of the week.",
"major-10|cups-05":"A hard turn has left you looking at what spilled. Grief is fair, but the wheel keeps moving, and so will your heart in time. Single, be patient with recovery and do not force a new start. Partnered, mourn together, and remember that a difficult season is not the whole story.",
"major-10|cups-06":"Memories stir as life turns another corner, and the sweetness in them is real. Enjoy it, then ask whether it fits the person you are now. Single, nostalgia can show what kind of gentleness you want. Partnered, share old photographs and laugh together at how far you have come.",
"major-10|cups-07":"Fortune is offering many romantic possibilities, and few are solid. Timing tempts you to grab the most glittering one. Slow down. Single, see who remains kind and consistent after the initial glow. Partnered, do not let fantasy about a different life distract you from the real one.",
"major-10|cups-08":"The season has changed, and part of you knows it. Walking away from what no longer fits is allowed, and the wheel will not carry you if you stay still. Single, leaving old patterns makes room. Partnered, speak honestly about the change you feel and listen to theirs.",
"major-10|cups-09":"A wish comes closer to being met, thanks partly to timing you did not control. Enjoy it without gripping. Single, satisfaction with your own life is an attractive place to stand. Partnered, appreciate how far you have come together, and remember good times can be renewed.",
"major-10|cups-10":"A fortunate turn settles into something lasting: home, family, a place among people who love you. Nothing here is guaranteed, but the direction is good. Single, community may be where love finds you. Partnered, mark milestones together and tend the everyday routines that keep a household warm.",
"major-10|cups-11":"A sweet surprise arrives, perhaps a message, perhaps a new feeling you did not plan for. Let it be small at first. Single, respond honestly and see where it goes. Partnered, a playful moment can lift a stale week. Keep your expectations light and your heart curious.",
"major-10|cups-12":"A romantic offer arrives on a turn of luck. It may be lovely, and it may be brief. Enjoy the invitation while noticing whether the person's actions match the charm. Single, say yes to the evening without writing the whole story. Partnered, revive some courtship and surprise each other.",
"major-10|cups-13":"Emotional depth remains steady while life changes around it. You or someone close offers a calm centre, and that is precious when circumstances shift. Single, trust your feelings but let them show over time. Partnered, be the calm one during a rough patch, and invite your partner to do the same.",
"major-10|cups-14":"Emotional maturity holds when life rearranges itself. Someone steady and kind, perhaps you, meets change without panic or control. Single, look for a calm character over dramatic chemistry. Partnered, respond to surprises with warmth and good sense, and remember you can only manage your own conduct, not every outcome.",
"major-11|major-12":"A fair decision cannot be rushed, so wait with open eyes. Consider your partner's viewpoint as carefully as your own. If you are single, a pause lets you see clearly what you owe yourself. When you do speak, your words will be balanced.",
"major-11|major-13":"An ending is the fair result of choices made, and it is time to accept it. Be honest about what happened and your part in it, without cruelty toward anyone. Closing the account cleanly lets you begin something new with clean hands.",
"major-11|major-14":"Fairness and gentleness balance each other. Talk about needs and limits in measured, honest words. Neither of you needs to win. If you are single, seek someone whose give and take feels even over time, not only at the start.",
"major-11|major-15":"Look honestly at an unequal arrangement. Something in the relationship, or in your pattern of choosing partners, keeps you tied to a bad deal. Seeing it clearly is the first step. You are allowed to ask for fairness and to step away from terms that never worked.",
"major-11|major-16":"A hard truth arrives suddenly and rearranges things. What was hidden is now visible, and consequences follow. It hurts, but it is also clarifying. Respond honestly, avoid revenge, and keep your integrity while you decide what to keep.",
"major-11|major-17":"Honesty leads to healing. Once you and your partner face what is true, hope grows naturally. If you are single, a fair look at past patterns clears the ground for gentler expectations. Trust is rebuilt by consistent, truthful acts, and it is possible.",
"major-11|major-18":"You are trying to judge something that is not yet clear. Avoid deciding on a mood or a partial story. Ask for the facts, listen without defending, and hold off on verdicts. Fairness needs good information, and the fog lifts with time.",
"major-11|major-19":"Honesty feels good here. Open, fair dealing brings warmth and ease. You and your partner can speak plainly without fear, and it draws you closer. If you are single, transparent people are the ones worth your time, and you can be one yourself.",
"major-11|major-20":"This is a moment of true accounting. You see what has happened and answer for it. Speak honestly, listen equally, and forgive where you can. It may reset the relationship on a truer footing, or help you close a chapter with clarity.",
"major-11|major-21":"Fair dealing has brought things to a satisfying whole. What you put in has been balanced by what you received. Enjoy the sense of completeness, and be grateful. If you are single, you carry a clear conscience into whatever comes next.",
"major-11|cups-01":"A new feeling deserves clear sight as well as delight. Enjoy it, and also notice whether it is fair, honest and mutual. Single, let a fresh connection prove itself through behavior. Partnered, a sincere, balanced gesture, one that gives as much as it asks, will renew trust.",
"major-11|cups-02":"Fairness is what makes this bond work. Each of you gives and receives in balance, and both are honest about it. Single, look for someone who treats you as an equal. Partnered, have the clear conversation about who does what, and be willing to adjust so both feel respected.",
"major-11|cups-03":"Being honest inside a happy circle is a skill. Friends may reflect back something true about a relationship. Single, listen when people who care about you say what they notice. Partnered, share the joy openly, and keep gossip and quiet comparisons out of the way.",
"major-11|cups-04":"Your restlessness deserves an honest audit. What exactly is missing, and is it fair to expect it? Single, weigh a kind offer on its merits, not on your mood. Partnered, tell the truth about your boredom without blaming, then choose one concrete step to improve things.",
"major-11|cups-05":"Consequences of a past choice are being felt, and grief is a natural response. Look honestly at your part without punishing yourself. Single, learning from what happened prepares you for a healthier bond. Partnered, apologize where you owe one and accept an apology sincerely offered.",
"major-11|cups-06":"Old hurts and old kindnesses both deserve a fair hearing. Looking back, you can see what was true and what was wishful. Single, use those lessons to choose more clearly. Partnered, settle an old imbalance by acknowledging it out loud, and let the sweetness of your shared history stay.",
"major-11|cups-07":"It is time to separate fantasy from fact. Many possibilities glow, but only some hold up when examined honestly. Single, judge people by what they do, not by what they promise or what you imagine. Partnered, be truthful about your daydreams and ask what is really missing at home.",
"major-11|cups-08":"Leaving can be the fair choice when you have weighed it honestly. Be clear about your reasons and kind in how you say them. Single, closing a chapter cleanly protects future connections. Partnered, if you are considering walking away, tell the truth first so nobody is left guessing.",
"major-11|cups-09":"Contentment that rests on honesty. You are satisfied because you have been straight with yourself and others. Single, integrity is part of your appeal. Partnered, enjoy a relationship where fairness is felt on both sides, and keep it that way with regular, open check-ins.",
"major-11|cups-10":"A happy home is built with fairness. Each person carries a fair share, and it shows in the warmth. Single, you may want a partnership like this and can look for it by valuing equality. Partnered, keep dividing responsibility and affection evenly, and thank each other often.",
"major-11|cups-11":"A tender, early feeling meets clear eyes. Enjoy the sweetness, and be honest about what you want and what the other person is offering. Single, answer a kind message sincerely and without games. Partnered, share a small vulnerability and encourage the same in return, fairly and gently.",
"major-11|cups-12":"A romantic offer meets a level-headed response. Charm is pleasant, but consistency is what you are weighing. Single, accept the invitation and watch whether words and actions match over a few weeks. Partnered, romance is best with honesty, so pair the flowers with a real conversation.",
"major-11|cups-13":"Compassion with clear boundaries. You or someone close feels deeply and is also honest about limits. Single, that combination is healthy and worth protecting. Partnered, say what you feel and what you need in the same breath, and trust that fairness and tenderness can sit together.",
"major-11|cups-14":"Feeling and judgement are in balance here. Someone, maybe you, is warm yet fair, generous yet honest about limits. Single, this mature steadiness is worth seeking and offering. Partnered, resolve disagreements by listening first and deciding together, without letting old grievances tip the scale.",
"major-12|major-13":"The pause and the ending belong together. Let go of the need to force outcomes. Something that no longer fits is dissolving, and resisting only prolongs the ache. Take a different view of what this loss makes possible, then step forward slowly.",
"major-12|major-14":"Patience is easy to say and hard to do, yet both cards ask for it. Let things develop at their own pace. Keep your side gentle and balanced while you wait, and be curious about your partner's rhythm. If you are single, unhurried connection is the healthy kind.",
"major-12|major-15":"Feeling stuck may be less about waiting and more about attachment. Ask whether you are pausing for a good reason or simply clinging to a pattern. A change of viewpoint can show that the chains are looser than they look.",
"major-12|major-16":"Sudden change forces you to stop and reconsider. Upheaval has interrupted the usual story. Rather than rushing to rebuild, hang in the uncomfortable pause and look at things from a new side. What seemed solid may have been a habit.",
"major-12|major-17":"Rest brings renewal. After an uncertain or tender time, you begin to feel hopeful without needing an answer. Allow yourself to trust slowly. If you are single, tending your own wellbeing is exactly the right thing to do right now.",
"major-12|major-18":"Waiting in the fog is uncomfortable. You do not have enough clarity and cannot force it. Try a different angle: write down your fears, then question each one. Give the situation time to reveal itself, and be patient with your own uncertainty.",
"major-12|major-19":"Here is a pause that turns out to be good. Letting go of control brings unexpected ease and warmth. Enjoy the stillness without demanding progress. If you are single, contentment while you wait draws better company than anxious searching does.",
"major-12|major-20":"A willing pause leads to an awakening. In the stillness you hear something honest about what you want. Answer it. It may mean forgiving a past hurt, or speaking up at last. Nothing needs to be forced: the call becomes clear when you listen.",
"major-12|major-21":"A voluntary wait has been worthwhile. Letting things unfold has led to a sense of completeness. Enjoy where you have arrived, and thank yourself for the patience. Whether you are single or partnered, you are ready for what comes next.",
"major-12|cups-01":"A new feeling arrives while you are in a pause, and that is helpful. You do not have to act on it right away. Single, look at the connection from a different angle before deciding what it means. Partnered, let a soft moment of affection simply be, without a plan.",
"major-12|cups-02":"Mutual affection is worth a patient approach. Willingly slowing down lets both people see each other more clearly. Single, do not rush to define it. Partnered, try looking at your disagreements from the other person's chair for a week, and notice what changes between you.",
"major-12|cups-03":"Friends may see your situation differently than you do, and their view is worth a hearing. Step out of the busy circle for a moment and reflect on what makes you happy. Single, patience with a slow-building connection pays. Partnered, celebrate without pressing for answers.",
"major-12|cups-04":"A stall in your feelings can be a useful pause rather than a problem. Sit with it and ask what the flatness is telling you. Single, do not force interest in an offer that leaves you cold, and do not dismiss one too quickly. Partnered, look at the routine from a fresh angle.",
"major-12|cups-05":"Grief slows everything down, and this time you are allowed to let it. Sit in the pause without hurrying to a resolution. Something looks different from this angle, and there is still something worth keeping. Single, rest. Partnered, be quietly present with each other and skip the arguments.",
"major-12|cups-06":"Looking at the past from a new angle changes its meaning. Old memories may show what you really needed or what was missing. Single, take your time and let gentle reflection settle old feelings. Partnered, revisit a shared memory and see it through your partner's eyes.",
"major-12|cups-07":"You are stuck between options and imagined futures. Pause is wise, but be honest about what the pause is for. Single, consider whether a fantasy is shielding you from a real, smaller possibility. Partnered, stop comparing your relationship to invented alternatives and look at what is actually here.",
"major-12|cups-08":"Leaving on purpose does not have to be fast. You may be choosing a deliberate pause, letting go of something while you consider what comes after. Single, that time alone can be healing. Partnered, be transparent that you need space to think, and set an honest framework for it.",
"major-12|cups-09":"Contentment can be found in the pause. You are not waiting for happiness to arrive. Single, enjoy the ease of your own company without feeling behind. Partnered, appreciate a slower season together and let a wish rest without pressing on it. What is offered now is already good.",
"major-12|cups-10":"This is patience chosen for the sake of belonging. You may be putting a personal wish on hold for the good of a family or partnership, and doing it willingly. Single, community can hold you while you wait. Partnered, make sure the sacrifice is mutual and voiced, not silent.",
"major-12|cups-11":"A tender message arrives while you are in a pause, and you can respond with thoughtful stillness. There is no rush. Single, look at a gentle overture from a few angles before replying. Partnered, a soft, curious question about how your person sees things can start a lovely conversation.",
"major-12|cups-12":"A romantic invitation arrives, and your instinct is to hold still and think. Good. Look at the offer from the other person's side and from your own. Single, you can say yes to coffee and no to hurry. Partnered, slow down enough to be really present on a date.",
"major-12|cups-13":"Deep feeling, held in stillness. You or someone close is willing to wait and listen rather than push. Single, your sensitivity gives you an unusual view of what a partner needs. Partnered, hold space for your person's feelings without trying to fix them, and let understanding form.",
"major-12|cups-14":"Calm and willing surrender to the moment. Someone, maybe you, does not need to control how love unfolds. Single, steady maturity means being at peace with waiting well. Partnered, listen fully before you respond, and be willing to see a conflict from your partner's side.",
"major-13|major-14":"After an ending, healing proceeds slowly. Do not hurry to fill the space. Mix rest with gentle activity, and allow trust to return in small doses. If you are in a relationship, changes may need gradual blending rather than a single dramatic break.",
"major-13|major-15":"Something is ending, and something else wants to keep you from letting it end. Notice the fear or habit that ties you to what is finished. Loosening that grip is painful and freeing. You deserve a life not built on obligation or repetition.",
"major-13|major-16":"This is a complete and sudden clearing. What ends does so abruptly and leaves little to hold. It is painful, and it is also honest. Give yourself space to grieve, avoid quick fixes, and rebuild only what is true when you are ready.",
"major-13|major-17":"After loss, hope. A quiet, tender renewal follows what has ended. You may be surprised how light you feel. Be open to gentle beginnings, and do not compare them to what was. If you are single, trust that new connection can arrive in its own way.",
"major-13|major-18":"An ending has left you in uncertainty. You are not sure what comes next, or what you truly feel. Let things stay unresolved for a while. Do not fill the gap with guesses. Journals, quiet walks, and honest talks with friends will help you see.",
"major-13|major-19":"Endings can be a relief. A weight is lifting, and you feel more like yourself. Enjoy the simple pleasure of a clear slate. If you are single, new warmth is possible. If you are partnered, letting an old pattern die can bring back real joy.",
"major-13|major-20":"This is a final accounting and a rebirth. See what has ended for what it was, forgive what you can, and answer the call to begin differently. It may involve a frank talk. You are allowed to become someone new.",
"major-13|major-21":"A cycle ends because it is complete, not because it failed. Honor what it gave you. You have grown, and you are ready for a new form of love, whether shared or solo. Let the close be peaceful, and thank the past for its part.",
"major-13|cups-01":"An ending clears the ground and a new feeling arrives in it. The heart opens after something has closed. Single, you can begin without carrying the old story. Partnered, a change in how you relate may be both a loss and a fresh start. Welcome the tenderness.",
"major-13|cups-02":"A bond is transformed rather than lost. What ended may be an old way of relating, so that something more honest and mutual can begin. Single, a fresh partnership can form once you release the old pattern. Partnered, renew your commitment on new terms that suit who you are now.",
"major-13|cups-03":"A season of social life is ending, and another is beginning. Friend groups shift, and so do the ways you meet people. Single, new circles bring new chances. Partnered, let go of old habits at gatherings and start new traditions. Mourn what changed and celebrate what is arriving.",
"major-13|cups-04":"Boredom may be telling you that something has run its course. Do not ignore it, and do not react rashly. Ask honestly whether the relationship needs an ending, a renewal or simply more attention. Single, letting go of old expectations can free you. Partnered, name the emptiness kindly.",
"major-13|cups-05":"Loss and endings meet, and the grief is deep. Let it be. Also notice that something remains behind you, and that a new phase will follow when you are ready. Single, healing is the task. Partnered, be gentle, since both of you may be mourning a change.",
"major-13|cups-06":"This is letting go of the past, sweetly. Memories can be honored and released at the same time. Single, an old attachment may finally loosen, making space for something in the present. Partnered, remember what was kind between you and let outdated grievances end while the good stays.",
"major-13|cups-07":"Illusion is being cleared away. Fantasies about love may end so that something real can begin. It can feel like a loss, and it is also relief. Single, drop the imagined ideal and meet real people. Partnered, set aside the what-ifs and put your attention on the person actually in front of you.",
"major-13|cups-08":"This is a deliberate ending. You know something has finished, and you choose to walk away with open eyes. Grief and relief can share the same day. Single, releasing an old attachment opens the road. Partnered, if a chapter is closing, do it honestly, without blame, and leave room for grief.",
"major-13|cups-09":"Satisfaction arrives after a clearing. You let something go, and there is unexpected ease on the other side. Single, being at peace after an ending is a good place to stand. Partnered, a period of change has passed and you can enjoy the calmer relationship that remains.",
"major-13|cups-10":"A stage of family or home life ends, and another takes its place. Children grow, households change, routines rearrange. Single, your idea of what belonging looks like may be transforming. Partnered, honor what the old chapter gave you and build new rituals for the next.",
"major-13|cups-11":"A tender new message arrives after an ending. It is a small beginning, and it is enough. Single, let something soft start without loading it with old hurts. Partnered, a simple, sincere gesture can mark a fresh chapter after a hard stretch. Go gently.",
"major-13|cups-12":"A romantic offer comes as an old chapter closes. Be honest with yourself about whether you have finished grieving. Single, invitations are welcome, and you can accept them at your own pace. Partnered, renewal may take the form of courtship again, with new plans, if both of you choose it.",
"major-13|cups-13":"This is a deep emotional transformation, handled with compassion. You or someone near you can grieve and grow at once. Single, honor your feelings about an ending, and trust that your capacity to love has not shrunk. Partnered, hold each other gently through a change of season.",
"major-13|cups-14":"Mature acceptance of an ending. Someone, perhaps you, can let go without bitterness and stay kind. Single, that emotional steadiness prepares you for a healthier bond. Partnered, handle a big change with calm and care, and be honest about what the two of you are leaving behind.",
"major-14|major-15":"Moderation is the antidote to a pattern that has you. Rather than swinging between craving and cutting off, look for the middle: healthy limits, honest talk, slow change. If you are single, notice whether excitement is hiding something unbalanced.",
"major-14|major-16":"A sudden break interrupts a calm patch. Answer with steadiness. Do not act on the first surge of feeling. Blend patience with honesty as you sort out what remains. Gentle, measured steps rebuild trust better than dramatic ones.",
"major-14|major-17":"Healing and hope work well together. Take things at a gentle pace, and let trust return naturally. If you are single, being kind to yourself sets the tone for what you attract. In a relationship, share small acts of care regularly.",
"major-14|major-18":"You feel unsure, and the cure is calm. Do not chase certainty through drama. Move slowly, ask gentle questions, and give feelings time to settle. Trust what stays consistent across days, rather than what flares at night.",
"major-14|major-19":"Ease and warmth arrive together. Things feel natural, balanced, and good. Enjoy simple routines shared with someone, or content time on your own. If you are single, relax: connections formed in good spirits tend to be sustainable.",
"major-14|major-20":"A gentle but real reckoning is here. Look at how you have been mixing your needs and your partner's over time, and adjust. The call is to be honest without harshness. Reconciling differences takes patience and clear words.",
"major-14|major-21":"Patient blending has led to wholeness. What you and someone else, or you and your own life, have been building slowly now feels complete. Appreciate it. Keep the small habits that got you here, because they are what made it last.",
"major-14|cups-01":"A new feeling arrives, and the best response is a slow, measured welcome. Let it mix with your daily life gradually. Single, pace yourself and enjoy the early warmth. Partnered, pour a little fresh affection into ordinary routines and see what the blend becomes over weeks.",
"major-14|cups-02":"Two people are learning to blend, giving and adjusting with good humor. Single, look for someone who is easy to be with and willing to meet halfway. Partnered, compromise is a craft, not a defeat. Small adjustments made regularly keep the connection flowing and the peace real.",
"major-14|cups-03":"Joy in moderation. A friendly gathering, a warm evening, a mix of company and calm. Single, social ease is an asset, so let people see your relaxed side. Partnered, balance time with friends and time as a couple so neither feels squeezed out. Everyone leaves happy.",
"major-14|cups-04":"Boredom can be treated with small, gentle adjustments rather than dramatic moves. Add a little variety to the routine and see what shifts. Single, try one new social habit at a time. Partnered, blend a bit of novelty into familiar comforts, and check in about what each of you is missing.",
"major-14|cups-05":"Healing takes a long middle, and that is normal. Grief and hope can share the same day. Single, let recovery proceed at its natural speed, with small kindnesses to yourself. Partnered, blend patience with honesty, be gentle when it gets heavy and steady through the quiet parts.",
"major-14|cups-06":"Old kindness and present life can be blended. Let memories inform how you love now without replacing it. Single, gentle nostalgia can show what tenderness means to you. Partnered, mix a favorite tradition from the past into today's rhythm, and enjoy how naturally the two fit together.",
"major-14|cups-07":"Many romantic ideas are swirling, and moderation helps you sort them. Take small steps and let reality mix into fantasy a little at a time. Single, meet people in ordinary settings. Partnered, blend your dreams with everyday life so imagination enriches the relationship instead of escaping it.",
"major-14|cups-08":"Walking away in a measured way. You are not storming off, you are leaving with care and a plan. Single, let the transition happen gradually, so you take your best self along. Partnered, if change is necessary, talk it through patiently and aim for an ending both of you can live with.",
"major-14|cups-09":"Contentment born from balance. You are comfortable because you have found a good rhythm between giving and receiving, closeness and independence. Single, you can enjoy this steadiness. Partnered, appreciate what you have built, and keep making the small adjustments that sustain it.",
"major-14|cups-10":"A harmonious home life takes ongoing tuning. Each person contributes a little and adjusts a little. Single, you may value gentle, stable connection above intensity, and that is a fine compass. Partnered, keep blending your needs, your family's needs and your own, with patience and humor.",
"major-14|cups-11":"A gentle new feeling, best given room to develop in small doses. Do not rush to name it. Single, reply kindly and let curiosity lead. Partnered, small, sincere gestures of affection blended into ordinary days will do more than a grand surprise. Let the feeling find its natural pace.",
"major-14|cups-12":"A romantic invitation is welcome, and moderation keeps it healthy. Enjoy the charm while letting the relationship deepen at a sensible speed. Single, say yes to a date without deciding what it means. Partnered, put romantic gestures into the regular week instead of saving them for special occasions.",
"major-14|cups-13":"Deep feeling, expressed in balance. You or someone near you is compassionate without being consumed, open without being overwhelmed. Single, that emotional evenness is attractive and rare. Partnered, give and receive care in similar amounts and share the emotional load fairly.",
"major-14|cups-14":"Emotional maturity, freely shared. Someone, maybe you, is warm, steady and fair, and knows how to keep a relationship in balance. Single, seek this quality and build it. Partnered, respond to strong feelings with patience, and find the moderate path when a disagreement heats up.",
"major-15|major-16":"A grip is broken suddenly. A pattern, a dependency, or a situation that felt inescapable collapses. It can be frightening and also freeing. Take care of yourself, be honest about what held you, and choose slowly what to build now.",
"major-15|major-17":"Hope shines on what has bound you. You can begin to loosen the pattern, and gentle self-care matters more than willpower. If you are single, believing you deserve better is a real starting point. Take one small, kind step away from what drains you.",
"major-15|major-18":"Fear and confusion feed each other here. Anxiety may distort what you see, and old habits pull you back. Get outside opinions from people you trust. Separate facts from fears. Clarity loosens the hold. You are free to take things slowly until the picture is clearer.",
"major-15|major-19":"Joy breaks a pattern. What once felt binding loses its power in honest warmth. Let simple, open happiness show you what you really want. If you are single, you no longer need to settle for what drains you.",
"major-15|major-20":"This is an honest awakening. You hear the call to leave a pattern behind, to forgive yourself, and to choose differently. Say what is true. Old bonds lose their force once you name them, and a new stage of life can begin.",
"major-15|major-21":"Freedom arrives at the end of a long tangle. The cycle is finishing, and you can stand on your own feet. Whatever bound you has run its course. Celebrate, and be careful not to recreate the same pattern in the next chapter.",
"major-15|cups-01":"A spark of real affection is offered, and part of you wants to grab it and hold on too tightly. Notice whether you are drawn to the person or to the relief they bring. Warmth that leaves you free to breathe is the kind worth accepting slowly.",
"major-15|cups-02":"Two people meet each other halfway, yet one habit keeps pulling the bond tight. Ask honestly whether the closeness is chosen or clung to. A partnership grows best when each person could walk away and still stays. Say that out loud to each other.",
"major-15|cups-03":"The party is lovely and the crowd is warm, but notice who you become in it. If a friend group keeps you in a familiar role, or a fling is more habit than joy, step outside for air. Real gladness survives a quiet night.",
"major-15|cups-04":"Boredom with what is in front of you meets a pattern that feels hard to leave. Before deciding the relationship is dull, ask whether the routine itself is the problem. Change one small habit together this week, and see what wakes up or what does not.",
"major-15|cups-05":"Grief over what spilled can harden into a loop where you replay the same hurt and stay near the same person or story. Let yourself mourn, then notice the two cups still standing. Choosing what remains is a gentler act than punishing yourself over what is gone.",
"major-15|cups-06":"Sweet memories tug at you, and an old bond or an old wound feels strangely comforting. Nostalgia is fine as a visit, less so as a home. Ask whether you long for the person or for how safe things once felt, then decide what you want now.",
"major-15|cups-07":"Fantasy and fixation mix here. You may be spinning a dozen versions of who someone could be while staying attached to none of them. Step back and look at the actual person, or the actual gap in your life, and ask what is real and steady.",
"major-15|cups-08":"Leaving on purpose is possible, and something is making it hard. A bond can be familiar without being good for you. If you feel the pull to walk away, take it seriously and get support from someone outside the situation. Going gently is still going.",
"major-15|cups-09":"Contentment is real here, but so is the risk of confusing indulgence with fulfillment. Enjoy what is good in your love life without letting comfort become the only thing you chase. If something is missing, say so kindly and trust that wanting more is allowed.",
"major-15|cups-10":"A warm, full home life is shown, along with the question of who is doing the holding together. Belonging feels best when nobody plays a role out of duty or fear. Take a real look at the family picture and gently adjust one pattern that no longer fits.",
"major-15|cups-11":"A tender message or a fresh flutter arrives, and an old attachment tugs at the sleeve. Be honest about which one deserves your attention. New feelings are shy and need room. Answer the kind note in your own time, and do not let history answer for you.",
"major-15|cups-12":"A romantic invitation arrives with polish and charm. Enjoy it, and check whether the pull feels like freedom or like a hook. Good courtship lets you say no without penalty. Let the pace be yours, and watch how the person treats your answer.",
"major-15|cups-13":"Deep feeling can steady you, and it can also cling. You may be the one who holds everyone's emotions, or you may be leaning hard on someone who does. Gentle limits are not coldness. Let love flow both ways and keep some of it for yourself.",
"major-15|cups-14":"Kindness with judgement matters most when a relationship has a strong hold on you. Steady, calm choices work better than dramatic ones. Talk to someone wise, and let care for yourself sit next to care for them. Being generous and being free are not opposites.",
"major-16|major-17":"Calm comes after the storm. What fell was false, and the quiet that follows brings hope. Heal gently and let trust rebuild slowly. If you are single, be kind to yourself and look forward. New beginnings are possible without denying what happened.",
"major-16|major-18":"A shock has left you unsure what is real. Shadows and worries multiply after a sudden change. Wait before drawing conclusions. Find steady people to talk with, and ask for facts. Your footing will return as things settle.",
"major-16|major-19":"The storm ends and light returns. What broke made room for something truer and warmer. Allow yourself relief and joy. If you are single, you may feel freer than you expected. If you are partnered, honesty after a rough moment can bring you closer.",
"major-16|major-20":"A sudden truth demands a response. Something broke, and now you must decide what it means. Hear the call honestly. This can be a painful but clean turning point, giving you a chance to start over with clearer values.",
"major-16|major-21":"A dramatic ending completes a long story. What falls now was ready to fall, and what remains is whole. Honor the journey. Whether you are single or partnered, you are entering a new phase with hard-won wisdom.",
"major-16|cups-01":"A sudden shake-up clears space, and a new tenderness is offered in the dust. Do not rush to build on it yet. Let the ground settle, then see if the feeling holds when things are quiet. Real openings can survive an ordinary Tuesday.",
"major-16|cups-02":"Something shakes a partnership, and how you meet each other in the aftermath tells the story. If you can stand in the mess together and be honest, the bond may come out truer. If one of you hides, the cracks stay. Speak first and plainly.",
"major-16|cups-03":"The party ends abruptly, or a group of friends is jolted by news. Your circle is a source of comfort while a personal shake-up settles. Lean on the ones who show up. Being seen at your messiest is how friendships, and sometimes romances, deepen.",
"major-16|cups-04":"A jolt wakes you from a stretch of dull withdrawal. Something had gone stale, and now you cannot ignore it. Instead of retreating further, notice what you have been refusing to look at. The change may hurt, and it also offers a fresh look at your heart.",
"major-16|cups-05":"Loss arrives with a jolt, and grief follows. Let yourself cry over the spilled cups and do not rush to a verdict about love itself. The collapse cleared away something false, even if it hurts. Two cups still stand behind you, waiting for when you turn.",
"major-16|cups-06":"An old memory or an old flame returns just as life is being rearranged. Nostalgia can comfort you, though it is not a map. Enjoy the sweetness without rewriting the past. Let the upheaval teach you what you actually need from love today.",
"major-16|cups-07":"A shock cuts through daydreams and idealized pictures. It hurts and it clarifies. You may see that a fantasy version of someone, or of your future, was not standing on anything solid. Ground yourself in what is actually said and done, and let the rest go.",
"major-16|cups-08":"The structure breaks, and you find the courage to walk away from something that was already hollow. Leaving is sad and also clean. Take only what you need and go at your own pace. Grief and relief can sit side by side, and both are allowed.",
"major-16|cups-09":"A wish you thought was nearly granted gets a shake. It may be a comfort zone rattled or a plan rearranged. If your contentment collapses, look at what it rested on. Happiness built on honesty can be rebuilt, and it often comes back sturdier.",
"major-16|cups-10":"A family or household is shaken, and everyone's sense of home wobbles. Belonging can survive the change if people talk honestly and share the load. This is a time for patience, clear conversations, and small rituals that remind everyone they are still a unit.",
"major-16|cups-11":"A tender message or a new spark shows up right after something big falls apart. It is easy to grab it as comfort. Let it be gentle and small for now. Feelings that appear in a crisis deserve time before you hand them a large role.",
"major-16|cups-12":"An attractive invitation arrives while your world is in flux. Enjoy the charm, but ask whether you are seeking connection or an escape hatch. Romance is more likely to grow when both people know your situation and go at a pace that feels honest.",
"major-16|cups-13":"Big waves hit, and your steady heart is the raft. You feel deeply and can hold others through a crisis, yet you also need holding. Let someone care for you while things settle. Emotional depth is a strength when it is shared, not carried alone.",
"major-16|cups-14":"In the middle of upheaval, a composed, kind response is your best gift to yourself and others. Feel what you feel, then choose words carefully. Steadiness is not coldness. It lets a difficult conversation happen without wounds that take years to heal.",
"major-17|major-18":"Hope shines through uncertainty. You might not have every answer, but a gentle faith persists. Follow your intuition carefully, and check it against real words and actions. If you are single, be open without being naive.",
"major-17|major-19":"Warmth, healing, and simple happiness are all present. Things feel bright and hopeful, and you deserve to enjoy them. If you are single, you radiate approachability. If you are partnered, spend time together doing what you both love.",
"major-17|major-20":"Hope answers a call. You feel ready to heal, forgive, and start fresh. Trust the inner voice urging you toward a more honest, open life. Speak your truth kindly, and let renewal begin. Whether you are single or partnered, the fresh start begins with how you treat yourself.",
"major-17|major-21":"Healing is complete, and hope has led somewhere whole. You feel at peace, whether partnered or on your own. Give thanks, share your contentment, and step into the next season with openness. Contentment you already feel is a good place to meet someone new or to grow closer to someone you have.",
"major-17|cups-01":"Hope and a new opening arrive together. After a hard stretch, your heart is ready for something honest and gentle. If you are single, let yourself be seen a little more. If partnered, offer a small, sincere gesture that says you still believe in this.",
"major-17|cups-02":"Healing and mutual care are on the table. Two people can quietly restore trust when each gives and receives fairly. Whether you are new or long together, share a hope out loud and ask for theirs. Gentle honesty is the repair that lasts.",
"major-17|cups-03":"Friends may be the medicine you need, and joy is allowed again. Go to the gathering, laugh at the old jokes, and let your heart soften. Romance or reconciliation might follow, though the point right now is being among people who wish you well.",
"major-17|cups-04":"After a disappointment, you may feel flat, and hope is quietly returning. Do not mistake this lull for the end. Gentle attention to what you already have, or to a new possibility just outside your gaze, can lift the fog. Look up when you feel ready.",
"major-17|cups-05":"Grief has passed through, and hope arrives like a calm evening. You can honor what was lost and still turn toward what remains. Tend to yourself first with rest, kind company, and small comforts. Your heart is healing, and it does not need to hurry.",
"major-17|cups-06":"Childhood sweetness and old kindness come back to you, and they are a source of healing rather than a trap. Remember who once loved you well and let that memory set your standard. Offer someone that same easy gentleness today.",
"major-17|cups-07":"Wishes are many, and hope is clearing the fog. Pick out which desires are truly yours and which are borrowed from films or friends. Choose one honest step toward the real one, like a candid conversation or a first coffee, and let the daydreams rest.",
"major-17|cups-08":"Walking away from something that no longer nourishes you can be an act of faith in what comes next. Leave without bitterness and carry the lessons. Night sky, quiet path, steady step: the way forward becomes visible as you move, one calm decision at a time.",
"major-17|cups-09":"Quiet satisfaction and a hopeful heart go together here. Enjoy what is good in your love life without rushing to fix it. If a wish for connection is close, keep showing up warmly and openly. Gratitude makes you easier to love and easier to be near.",
"major-17|cups-10":"Belonging comes into view after a long stretch of doubt. Family, chosen or born, can be a place of ease. If you are single, remember that home can be built from friends and small rituals. If partnered, plan something simple that celebrates what you share.",
"major-17|cups-11":"Something soft and sincere is reaching for you: a kind text, a small confession, a shy glance. Meet it with the same honesty. If you are the one who feels the first flutter, say it simply and let the other person answer freely.",
"major-17|cups-12":"An honest, romantic invitation may come, and you are in a good place to answer it. Take your time, ask real questions, and see how the person listens. Hope makes you generous, so let your standards stay clear and your yes, or no, be genuine.",
"major-17|cups-13":"You are emotionally steady and open, which is a rare and attractive mix. Trust your intuition about people, and let yourself be cared for as well. A calm heart can hear the truth in a conversation, so listen closely and answer kindly.",
"major-17|cups-14":"Mature, kind, well-judged love is the theme. You know how to feel deeply without being ruled by it. Offer honest support, keep your word, and let others see your gentleness. If you seek a partner, look for the same steady warmth you offer.",
"major-18|major-19":"The fog lifts and you see clearly. Worries that seemed large turn out to be manageable. Speak plainly about what confused you, and enjoy the relief. If you are single, trust yourself more. If you are partnered, honest talk brings warmth.",
"major-18|major-20":"A quiet call rises from the depths. Your dreams and feelings are pointing to something you can no longer ignore. Listen, and then act on it with care. Talk honestly, and let the fog clear as you speak.",
"major-18|major-21":"You are nearly there, though some doubts remain. Finish the current stage without letting vague worries spoil it. Enjoy what is real. Whole and satisfied feelings are possible even when a few questions stay unanswered.",
"major-18|cups-01":"Someone offers affection while you cannot yet see the whole picture. Feelings are real, but the story around them is hazy. Ask simple questions, notice what stays the same over weeks, and let clarity arrive before you build anything large on it.",
"major-18|cups-02":"Two people are drawn together, yet each may be projecting hopes onto the other. Take off the rose-colored filter. Talk about ordinary things: schedules, values, how you handle stress. A bond that feels magical becomes lasting when it meets daylight.",
"major-18|cups-03":"The social scene is lively, but your read on someone in it is blurry. Party charm and late-night talk can distort things. Give a new interest time in ordinary settings, and listen to what friends who know you well notice about how you act around them.",
"major-18|cups-04":"You feel restless or numb, and your own mood is hard to read. Are you bored, tired, or protecting yourself? Before you decide anything about a relationship, spend a few days on sleep, movement, and honest journaling. Fog lifts faster when you tend the basics.",
"major-18|cups-05":"Sorrow and uncertainty travel together. You may be grieving something you do not fully understand, or imagining the worst in the dark. Talk to someone you trust and check your assumptions. Night distorts, and morning often shows a gentler and clearer outline.",
"major-18|cups-06":"Memory glows softly, and so does the tendency to edit the past. Enjoy the warmth of what once was, but check whether you are remembering the whole story. Let the old kindness remind you what you value, then look toward who and what is actually in front of you.",
"major-18|cups-07":"Illusions abound. You may be picturing several futures at once, and none is grounded in what people have actually said or done. Slow down. Write what you know as fact, set aside the rest, and pay attention to steady behavior over dreamy possibility.",
"major-18|cups-08":"You sense it is time to leave a situation, but the reasons are not fully clear. Trust that quiet knowing, and give yourself time to sort out the details. Talk to a trusted friend. A calm exit, planned with care, protects your heart better than a midnight impulse.",
"major-18|cups-09":"Contentment is present, with a whisper of doubt beneath it. Enjoy the good moments while staying honest about what you may be avoiding. A relationship or single life that feels pleasant deserves a check-in now and then, so nothing important stays unspoken.",
"major-18|cups-10":"Family life or a long-term bond looks warm from the outside, with some undercurrents that have not been named. Gently ask what each person needs. Bring quiet worries to the table and listen with care. Belonging deepens when hidden feelings are welcome.",
"major-18|cups-11":"Butterflies show up, and so does uncertainty about what the message really means. Enjoy the sweetness, then ask a clear, friendly question instead of decoding every emoji. Fresh feelings need daylight and simple words to become something you can rely on.",
"major-18|cups-12":"A romantic gesture arrives, and something about it feels a little unreal. Enjoy the attention while watching for consistency. Charm shows its depth over time. Notice whether actions match words across several weeks, and let your comfort level set the pace.",
"major-18|cups-13":"Your intuition is strong and your feelings run deep, which can make the fog feel more intense. Trust what you sense, then verify it with gentle questions. You do not have to carry every emotion in the room. Rest, and let understanding surface at its own pace.",
"major-18|cups-14":"Emotional maturity helps you stay calm while things are unclear. Resist deciding too soon. Be kind, ask for honesty, and offer it back. Someone who handles uncertainty with patience is a safe person to love, so be that for yourself first.",
"major-19|major-20":"Joy and honesty combine. You are ready to embrace a truer way of loving. Forgive, speak openly, and celebrate. If you are single, awakening to your own worth draws warm and sincere connection. If you are in a relationship, say out loud what you are grateful for in each other.",
"major-19|major-21":"Happiness and wholeness arrive at once. You feel content, celebrated, and complete. Whether you are single or partnered, savor it and share it with people you trust. Say thank you out loud. Gratitude keeps good things bright.",
"major-19|cups-01":"Openness and warmth pair beautifully. A real invitation to connect is available, and you can answer with confidence. Be plain and cheerful about what you want. Affection offered in daylight has nothing to hide, and that makes it easy to trust.",
"major-19|cups-02":"Mutual joy is the headline. Two people are meeting in the light, with easy honesty and shared delight. Keep it simple: spend time, laugh, say what you appreciate. If you are single, this shows you what a good partnership feels like, and that it exists.",
"major-19|cups-03":"Celebration is in the air. Friends, community, and cheerful company lift your heart. Say yes to invitations, share your good news, and let people love you. Romance may bloom in the glow of a happy crowd, or you may simply enjoy being well surrounded.",
"major-19|cups-04":"Light is shining on something you have overlooked. You may be so used to a person or a situation that you forgot how good it is. Lift your head, notice the small offering in front of you, and let gratitude replace the shrug of habit.",
"major-19|cups-05":"Loss is real, and so is the light on the other side. Let yourself grieve the spilled cups, then turn around and see what still stands. Warmth is returning to your days. Reach for people and simple joys, and let healing be uncomplicated.",
"major-19|cups-06":"Sweet memory and present happiness meet. Childlike joy, old kindnesses, and easy laughter are available now. Enjoy them without worrying about what they mean. Share a memory with someone you care about, and make one new good memory this week.",
"major-19|cups-07":"Daylight sorts out the daydreams. With clear eyes, you can tell which hopes are grounded in real people and which are pure fantasy. Choose the warm, honest option in front of you, and trust that a simple, sunny yes beats a hundred maybes.",
"major-19|cups-08":"Leaving what no longer serves you is easier under clear light. You can walk away with dignity, warmth, and no need to vilify anyone. Move toward what feeds your spirit. Where you are headed may be brighter than the road you are leaving behind.",
"major-19|cups-09":"Deep contentment is available: the wish comes true in a gentle, plain way. Savor it without needing to prove it. Whether single or partnered, look over the good in your life and say thank you out loud. Happiness that is acknowledged tends to grow.",
"major-19|cups-10":"Family joy and lasting togetherness are the picture. Home feels warm, and people are glad to see each other. If it is not there yet, build it in small pieces: shared meals, honest talk, reliable presence. A loving circle starts with someone showing up.",
"major-19|cups-11":"Sweet, sincere feelings show up without games. Say what you mean in a warm message, and accept the same from someone else. Early affection needs no grand plan, only honesty and a little courage. Let joy be simple and let yourself smile about it.",
"major-19|cups-12":"Romance arrives in an open, friendly way, with no need to guess. Someone may invite you out, or you might do the inviting. Go with an easy, daytime kind of plan. Honest enthusiasm from both sides is a fine start, and pace can stay relaxed.",
"major-19|cups-13":"Emotional warmth and steadiness make you a safe, radiant presence. Loving well means listening, being honest, and keeping your own center. Let people feel your care without absorbing their storms. In a partnership, this is the kind of tenderness that lasts through ordinary days.",
"major-19|cups-14":"Generous, mature affection is on display. You can be open-hearted and sensible at once. Offer support that respects the other person's choices, and speak plainly about your needs. Relationships thrive when kindness and good judgement work together in daily life.",
"major-20|major-21":"This is the final answer to a long question. You heard the call, responded honestly, and now a cycle completes. Enjoy the peace of no longer wondering. New beginnings can follow from this settled place.",
"major-20|cups-01":"A call arrives from the heart, and it asks for an honest response. Consider what you truly want rather than what feels safe or expected. If an offer of affection is on the table, answer it cleanly, with a real yes or a kind no.",
"major-20|cups-02":"Mutual truth-telling can renew a partnership. Sit down together and review what has worked and what has not, with kindness. If you are single, an honest look at your patterns prepares you to meet someone halfway. Either way, clarity is an act of care.",
"major-20|cups-03":"Your friends may see something you have not yet admitted. Listen to those who care about you, and let their honest view help you decide. Celebrate what is good, and be willing to say aloud what needs to change. Gladness is sturdier after an honest talk.",
"major-20|cups-04":"Restlessness is calling you to look at your situation honestly. Are you bored, or is something real being ignored? Answer yourself plainly. A wake-up moment can lead to renewed effort, a new conversation, or a decision to stop drifting.",
"major-20|cups-05":"An honest reckoning with grief helps you stop looping. Look at what happened without excuses or harsh self-blame. Learn what you can, forgive what you can, and let the rest go. Turning around to see what remains is the beginning of healing.",
"major-20|cups-06":"The past comes up for review, sweetly and seriously. Honor the good, and see clearly what belongs in the past. You may hear from someone from your history, or reflect on old patterns. Decide what to carry forward and what to lay down with thanks.",
"major-20|cups-07":"Time to sort what is real from what is wishful thinking. Take an honest inventory of your hopes and what people have actually shown you. Choose the path that matches reality, and release fantasies that keep you from a good, solid connection.",
"major-20|cups-08":"A clear inner call says it is time to go. You have reviewed the situation honestly, and your answer is arriving. Leave with care for yourself and respect for others. Trust that stepping away for good reasons can be an act of integrity and hope.",
"major-20|cups-09":"An honest look at your life shows a good deal to be glad about. Give thanks, and also name any quiet wish you have set aside. Contentment grows when you tell the truth about what you have and what you still hope for.",
"major-20|cups-10":"Family patterns come up for a fresh look. Which traditions are you happy to carry on, and which would you like to change? Honest conversations can renew a household or a long-term partnership. Belonging deepens when people are free to tell the truth.",
"major-20|cups-11":"A tender message deserves a direct answer. If something is stirring in you, say so with kindness and clarity. Early feelings ask for honesty and courage more than strategy. Take a quiet moment to check what you feel, then reply from that place.",
"major-20|cups-12":"An invitation arrives, and it calls for a clear answer. Consider what you want, and reply with candor and warmth. A romantic gesture is best met with your real feelings, whether that is enthusiasm, curiosity, or a kind decline. Honesty respects both people.",
"major-20|cups-13":"Deep feeling meets honest self-review. Listen to your inner voice, and let it guide a heartfelt conversation. You may need to release an old story about yourself. Meeting your own emotions with fairness makes it easier to love and be loved.",
"major-20|cups-14":"Wise, compassionate judgement is called for. Look at your relationships with kindness and honesty, then act on what you see. Be firm without being harsh. People remember how you treated them at a turning point, so choose words that you will be proud of.",
"major-21|cups-01":"A new chapter opens, and it begins with a real offering of the heart. You have reached a point where love can be received fully. If single, that might mean feeling ready. If partnered, it may mean a shared milestone or renewed vows of another kind.",
"major-21|cups-02":"A full, balanced partnership is within view. Two people meeting as equals, each whole on their own, can create something complete. Celebrate what you have built or are building. If you are single, this is a sign that mutuality is worth waiting for.",
"major-21|cups-03":"Celebration marks a milestone. Gather your people to mark an engagement, an anniversary, or a personal victory. Being surrounded by support helps you feel the completion. If single, enjoy the fullness of friendships and know your life is already rich.",
"major-21|cups-04":"You have arrived somewhere, and it may feel oddly quiet. That flat feeling can be the pause after a big stretch. Rest, then look around at what you built. A new desire will show up when you make space for it, so do not rush to fill the silence.",
"major-21|cups-05":"An ending completes, and grief is part of the closing. Honor what was, and let yourself feel the loss fully. The circle is finished, which means you are free to begin another. The two cups still standing show that your capacity for love remains.",
"major-21|cups-06":"You have come full circle, and old kindness returns in a new form. A reunion of spirit with your past, or with your younger self, helps you love more freely now. Bring that warmth into the present relationship or into how you treat yourself.",
"major-21|cups-07":"After many possibilities, one path feels whole. You have finished sampling and are ready to commit to something real. Choose the connection or way of life that matches your values, and let the other daydreams fade with gratitude for what they taught you.",
"major-21|cups-08":"You have finished what you came to do in a particular situation, and moving on feels natural and whole. Walk away with thanks rather than bitterness. Carrying lessons and warmth forward, you are ready for a wider chapter of your life.",
"major-21|cups-09":"Fulfillment is here. The wish has come true in some meaningful way, and you can rest in it. Let yourself feel satisfied, and share the feeling with people you love. If something is still missing, name it calmly, without spoiling what is already good.",
"major-21|cups-10":"A deeply fulfilling life picture comes into view: love, home, and community in balance. Whether it is a family, a partnership, or a circle of friends, you can feel that you belong. Appreciate it fully, and keep nurturing it in ordinary, daily ways.",
"major-21|cups-11":"Something tender begins as a larger cycle closes. You have room in your heart for new feelings, and they may arrive as a gentle message or a shy smile. Let the newness be small and sweet, and remember that completion made this space.",
"major-21|cups-12":"You arrive at a place where a romantic invitation feels welcome rather than urgent. Because you are whole on your own, you can say yes or no freely. Enjoy the courtesy and charm, and respond in the way that suits the life you have built.",
"major-21|cups-13":"Emotional wisdom has ripened, and you can love with depth and steadiness. You understand your own heart and can hold others gently. This is a sign of a mature, fulfilled way of relating. Offer it freely, and let yourself be received in return.",
"major-21|cups-14":"Emotional mastery and completion go together. You know how to feel deeply and act wisely. Offer that steadiness to a partner or to yourself, and speak with generosity and clarity. A love shaped by kindness and good judgement is a fine place to arrive."};
